(24844,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'May you find what you\'re looking for, $gbrother:sister;.',0),
(24845,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'May you find what you\'re looking for, $gbrother:sister;.',0),
(24846,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'May you find what you\'re looking for, $gbrother:sister;.',0),
(24847,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'May you find what you\'re looking for, $gbrother:sister;.',0),
(24848,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You... You\'re not Snivel. Did he send you? He\'s so late, I had started to give up hope...$B$B<Tears start welling up in the woman\'s eyes once she realizes that you aren\'t there to deliver a message from Snivel.>$B$BThat\'s not like my Snivel, but what choice is there?',0),
(24849,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'All he talked about was leaving town with all his money? Then he really has abandoned me, hasn\'t he?$B$BOh, $N. I was such a fool to fall for him, but how could I help myself? He was so irresistible!',0),
(24850,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'re not Snivel. He was supposed to be here an hour ago! What have you done with him?$B$B<Roka seems to calm down when you tell her that you\'re looking for Snivel, too. Then the tears start to well up in her eyes.>$B$BThis isn\'t like my Snivel. Do you think something\'s happened to him?',0),
(24851,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'All he talked about was leaving town with all his money? Then he really has abandoned me, hasn\'t he?$B$BI can\'t believe I fell for such a horrible goblin! But he was so irresistible when we first met.',0),
(24852,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thanks to you, our people are free to fight for our home.',0),
(24854,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Zen\'Aliri was wise to send you here. I\'ve hit a dead end in my studies.',0),
(24855,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The scent of bloodpetal pollen hangs about your head, $C. This is good.$B$BYou\'ve earned your reward.',0),
(24856,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Boss, we gotta problem.',27602),
(24857,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is quite alarming indeed! But with this information we can call on our brethren from Bloodhoof Village to help thwart the attack. You have saved the lives of many $r, $N.',0),
(24858,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I wish I could have seen the looks on their scaly faces when you blew up their banners and replaced them with our own.$B$BOn second thought, I don\'t want to be close enough to see their snarls.',27602),
(24859,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'We\'re going to be filthy rich, I tell you! Well, if we can get off of this island, that is.',27602),
(24861,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'There is balance in all things. As Greatmother Hawkwind\'s spirit takes its final journey, you will begin your first.',15595),
(24862,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'They\'re ambushing the roads to Stonetalon, too? We just can\'t get a break here. Where are they coming from, anyways?',0),
(24863,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What ... our supplies? These were meant for Stonetalon.\n\nNo matter, at the rate we\'re going, we need them more here. Honor\'s Stand has been cut off from the coast, $N. Commander Singleton is at his wit\'s end.',0),
(24864,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh, they\'re so cute! I wish that we could turn them into little plush toys and sell them for a gazillion macaroons!',27602),
(24865,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh... wow... it\'s some really old food. Hey Hol\'anyee, take a look at this! This $R brought us those old rations that we abandoned!$B$BNo, not from Marshal\'s Refuge... from the old base camp!$B$B$B$BI\'m not sure I want to peek inside. I\'ll just give it to Nolen, I guess... he\'ll know what to do with it.',0),
(24866,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well I\'ll be... that\'s Shizzle\'s old portable dinomometer! Where did you find this?$B$BI\'m surprised it\'s still functional, even after all these years. I\'ll have it delivered to Shizzle promptly.',0),
(24868,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'A faceless of the deep? What\'s that? That does NOT sound like a naga!$B$BWell, you killed it, whatever it was. It doesn\'t matter now. We have other fish to fry....',27602),
(24871,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The giant is dead? Praise the Light!$B$BThe way onward and upward is clear. Take some of these spoils of the battle as a token of our gratitude, and we will drink together in celebration once the Frozen Throne has been ground to dust!',0),
(24873,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'At last, we have live specimens to study! You have helped to save countless lives this day, $N.$B$BPlease, take this as a token of thanks for this great deed.',0),
(24897,5,18,0,0,0,1000,0,0,'$n? We\'re saved!$B$BWho am I kidding? We\'re all going to die!!!',27602),
(24901,396,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Okay, I think that\'s good enough for now, but they took a bunch of the townsfolk captive.$B$BWe\'re going to have to take the fight to them!',27602),
(24902,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The Plague?  Something so heinous that not even the orcs condone its use?  I\'d say this warrants notifying King Greymane.',25549),
(24903,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You present me with the most difficult choice of my life, $n.',25549),
(24904,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'We\'ve driven the Forsaken back.  We hold three out of the four districts.$B$BBut at what cost...',25549),
(24905,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I\'ve got a great one for you this time, $n. We\'re gonna initiate these ogres into the Horde...working directly under us.',0),
(24906,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hmm, mostly usable. This is good stuff. I\'ve already got buyers lined up, of course.$B$BHere\'s your advance for the rest of the work you\'re gonna do for me and the Bilgewater Cartel...partner.',0),
(24907,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Property values have already gone up since you left. People like seafront views that don\'t include briny, gnarled giants stomping around.$B$BHere\'s your cut, $n.',0),
(24910,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Isn\'t it nice when you can do a good deed, and see enormous future financial gains from it? It warms my little goblin heart. And my big goblin wallet.$B$BYou did great, kid. Gadgetzan\'s gonna be ours soon. Here\'s a little token of my appreciation.',0),
(24911,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hey Hol\'anyee, look at the getup on this one!$B$B<Williden turns to face you.>$B$BAhem. Our recruiter sent you? Good. Let\'s start out with a bit of honesty: Un\'Goro isn\'t the perfect nirvana that you may have been promised. You\'ve probably figured that out on the way over here, though.$B$BShall we get to work?',0),
(24912,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Stand Clear, $C, and steady yourself.',0),
(24913,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I am moved, $n. Prophet Velen has been in closely guarded seclusion. He has dared not waste his energy on anything save preparing for the final confrontation he has foretold.$B$BAnd yet, he came here, in person, to comfort a single dying soul.$B$BI must thank you as well, for helping me make my last effort to comfort my friend. My research will continue... and I hope that Magtoor will continue to watch over me.',0),
(24914,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<After tracing a complex pattern of runes on each of the box\'s surfaces, the outline of a lid appears and a click echoes through the chamber.>$B$BHere you are, $R.',0),
(24915,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Impossible...$B$BFather, is it you?!$B$BYou have done me a great service, hero. I offer you the reins of my faithful steed. Do with it as you please, but do not forget those that assisted you in this monumental feat.',0),
(24916,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What... how did you manage to come by this!?$B$BYou have done me a great service, hero. My heart could not bear to keep this locket, but I will place an enchantment upon it that you may find useful. Do with it as you please, but do not forget those that assisted you in this monumental feat.',0),
(24917,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Aye. I know this blade... and I will treasure it always - a moment of time that will be lost forever.$B$BYou have done me a great service, hero. I offer you a gift from the Frostborn dwarves. Do with it as you please, but do not forget those that assisted you in this monumental feat.',0),
(24918,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Sylvanas silently reflects for a moment before returning her gaze to you.>$B$BYou have done me a great service, hero. I offer you the boon of the Banshee Queen. Do with it as you please, but do not forget those that assisted you in this monumental feat.',0),
(24919,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Uther stares at the medal, speechless for a moment.>$B$BArthas\' medal.$B$BI remember well the day I presented it to him...$B$BYou have done me a great service, hero. My soul may now rest in peace. I offer you a memory lost in time. Do with it as you please, but do not forget those that assisted you in this monumental feat.',0),
(24920,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve done well, $n.  Almost everybody managed to make it through.  ',25549),
(24921,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hm? What unit are you with, $C?$B$BNo matter, we need all hands. My fleet is in tatters and they\'ve broken into the hold. You armed? That\'s good enough for me.',0),
(24924,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'$n? What are you doing wearing that pygmy helm? Looks like it\'s about to fall apart.$B$BI\'m glad that they sent you up here. I thought for sure they were going to send that jerk, Grapplehammer and his ego-enabling assistant.',27602),
(24925,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Great job, but that\'s not even half of the hostages that they took from town.$B$BDarn it all! They must have taken the rest of the captives to their other villages up in the volcano!',27602),
(24926,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'She decided to stay? Fascinating... I\'ll have to look over this data and find out why.$B$BThank you again, $n. I really appreciate it.',0),
(24927,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I\'m pleased to report that our brand recognition in this area has skyrocketed now that you\'ve killed most of the people who didn\'t want us here.',0),
(24928,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Wonderful job. Have you ever thought about becoming a full-time arsonist? I know a few people, it\'s a nice gig.$B$BWell, we\'ll chit-chat about that one later. More to do here!',0),
(24929,273,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Nice work, $g bud : girlfriend;! Hope he wasn\'t too tough.',27602),
(24930,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'If I hadn\'t seen you kill a few of the mangy things with my own eyes, I\'d think you did not complete the task I asked of you.$B$BIt looks like we\'re hardly putting a dent in their numbers.',25549),
(24931,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ahh, perfect! Just what I need...full of potent focusing energies...$B$B...ahem! I mean, perfect for my collection! Narain Soothfancy is in no need of artificial enhancement of any kind!$B$BNow take your pay and be off!',0),
(24932,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This isn\'t goin\' fast enough. There\'s gotta be a faster way...',0),
(24933,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Man, this stuff looks delicious. I\'m half tempted to just fry some up myself.$B$BNo! We\'ve gotta focus on gettin\' out of here.$B$BMaybe just one piece...',0),
(24934,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You make a hell of a marine, $n.$B$BWe\'ll mop up the others. But it looks like the Horde fleet is disengaging - maybe to land more troops ashore?$B$BAdmiral Aubrey will know what to do. Talk to me when you\'re ready to fly back!',0),
(24937,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'They turned some of our people into zombies? Tell me something I don\'t know....',27602),
(24938,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Aubrey sent you? Good! I take it you know your way around a cannon?',0),
(24939,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ho ho! The beach is ours!\n\nWe just might keep a foothold on this miserable dustball of a continent after all.',0),
(24940,71,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'My star player has arrived!',27602),
(24941,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The Horde is massing at the base of the hill. Breathlessly, you stuff the debris you collected into the muzzle of the cannon, step back, cover one ear, and tug on the igniter cord...',0),
(24942,71,16,0,0,0,1000,0,0,'You did it! No more zombies to worry about. Let\'s pause a moment in silence for the stinky departed.$B$BOkay, done.',27602),
(24943,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Great work! We\'ve knocked them on their heels, maybe long enough to shore up our defenses.\n\nProvided we find a way to take out their artillery...',0),
(24944,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'A steady stream of the walking wounded have come up the hill to see me, $N. I trust that was your work? Well done!',0),
(24945,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I gotta tell you, that\'s a load off of my mind. That is, I won\'t have to worry about no new zombies coming after my brains!',27602),
(24946,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This will do. In fact, it\'s more than we need. I devised an ingenious idea for a weapon that the boots will be turned into once you get them to Hobart.$B$BHand the powder over and I\'ll load it into the Super Booster Rocket Boots.',27602),
(24947,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good thing you\'re here! I\'m gonna need a lot of help if we want to beat these gnomes to the punch.',0),
(24948,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good! Without heavy equipment, the Horde will have to pull back to regroup. We\'ve bought ourselves some time to re-secure the fortress. Well done!',0),
(24949,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Beautiful! And to think these idiots were just sitting on it.$B$BHere\'s a bit up front, we\'ll talk about profit-sharing bonuses later.',0),
(24950,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Sea giants? You think he was training them towards Gadgetzan on purpose?$B$BWhatever, he\'s splitsville now. And Gadgetzan owes us big time! I can\'t wait to see the look on Marin\'s face.$B$BHere\'s your cut, babe. You\'re moving up in the world.',0),
(24951,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Look at the size of it! It\'s glorious. This ugly sucker\'s gonna help us bring down the whole hive.',0),
(24952,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'There\'s no time to waste, $G boy : girl;!$B$BWhat\'s wrong with the actuator on the left boot?!',27602),
(24953,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh man, that was awesome! You should\'ve seen the flames coming out of the hive!$B$BHere\'s your reward, for entertaining me as much as for clearing the hive!',0),
(24954,1,0,0,0,1000,0,0,0,'Careful with those glands, $n, careful!$B$B<Grapplehammer\'s eyes light up at the sight of the fiery organs.>$B$BAnd now to load them into the refashioned shredder boot. I\'m certain that you\'ll be surprised and amazed by my genius invention.',27602),
(24955,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Wow, nice work! I\'m amazed you even got them to hold a pen without eating it.$B$BYou can uh, just throw the suit over there. Away from me. In the fire.',0),
(24956,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Tolliver grasps the helmet reverently with quivering hands.>\n\nRageroar\'s battleships intercepted our vessel as we fled from Gilneas. We were to be carried here as trophies to the Warchief. As we neared the shore, some of us fought back. Rageroar - he began killing indiscriminately - howling with laughter. Our ship capsized and he ordered his men to fire at us as we drowned. Few of us made it to land.\n\nAfterwards, I learned that he wore my brother\'s scalp as... as a trophy.\n\n<He closes his eyes.>',0),
(24957,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ugh! This entire camp is like a sampler course of awful smells.$B$BLet\'s not handle these things any longer than we have to.',0),
(24958,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I managed to get everyone else safely back to town.$B$BJump in, we gotta get out of here before the volcano blows for good!!!',27602),
(24959,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hello there.  You must be... $N?',15595),
(24960,396,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve done well, $c.  As you can see, not all of us have resigned to our fates.  I\'m glad to see that you\'re at least willing to work.$b$bValdred will be a valuable asset to the Forsaken.  As for the other two... there is not much we can do.  We cannot force them to join us.',15595),
(24961,6,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You say she ran away?  What a shame.$b$bVery well.  As long as she\'s maintained her free will, there\'s still hope.',15595),
(24962,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I will be here to train you as you grow in experience... find me as often as you like. I charge a minimal fee, but you\'ll find everything I can teach you to be worthwhile.$B$BGo now and test your skill. Many more things will become known to you as you gain experience, some of which I am unable to discuss with you here. Just know that Sylvanas will need hunters with your type of cunning in the future.$b$bYou will be the backbone of our salvation. Do not forget it.',0),
(24963,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good job, you\'ve taught half the ogres here to fear and respect anything vaguely $R-shaped.$B$BIt\'s amazing what a little reward will do to keep people under your thumb, isn\'t it? Here\'s your payment, by the way.$B$B...what\'s with that look?',0),
(24964,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You seem to be somewhat of a natural, $n.  This is good.  I can\'t teach you everything myself.$b$bGo, practice what we\'ve discussed today.  Return when you\'re stronger, and we\'ll cover some more tricks and abilities.',0),
(24965,1,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I\'ve got to admit, the spell I just taught you probably won\'t increase your intellect severalfold.  That was a lie to get you to buy my services.  But it will still be a helpful spell for you and your allies.$b$bNo hard feelings!',15595),
(24966,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'re a good student, $n.  You\'ll go far.  If you ever need any further training, return to me and I\'ll happily oblige.',0),
(24967,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Trust me, this\'ll be worth the money. And hey - if you need any more training, stop by any time.',0),
(24968,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Congratulations... you\'re one step closer to being a master of the dark arts.  Go practice a bit, and return when you\'re stronger.  I\'ll have more to teach you then. ',0),
(24969,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You have the makings of a great $C, $n. Go, practice what we\'ve discussed, and return when you are stronger. Then I may have more to teach you.',0),
(24970,66,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'$N.  You made it.$b$bYou see those tents up there?  That\'s where we\'re headed.  The battle\'s probably already started.',15595),
(24971,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Being born again under the power of a val\'kyr is a strenuous process.  Many don\'t survive the shock, turning into zombies or ghouls.$b$bOthers retain just enough humanity to seem normal on the outside... but they\'re sick inside.  We should have slain those rotbrains the day they were raised.$b$bAs for you... you\'re a strong $c, $n.  I knew you\'d do well.  You\'ll be headed out of Deathknell soon.',15595),
(24972,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Yes, this is very good. You\'ve done well in obtaining this information, $n. Hmm... names of the Scarlet Crusade officers in the Tirisfal Glades...$b$bImagine the blow we could deal to the morale of those bloody zealots if we were to kill their leaders in one swift strike.  I will pass this information forward.',15595),
(24973,1,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well, it\'s a start.  It\'ll take a few weeks or months to fully clean out the infestation.  After that, we\'ll have to get down there with some torches to burn away the webbing.$b$bYou\'ve done your duty well, $n.',15595),
(24974,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh, look at him!  Isn\'t he the most adorable thing you\'ve ever seen?  Thank you, $n.  I feel more energetic already.',15595),
(24975,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You have performed your bidding well, young $c.  You are proving yourself to be quite an asset to the Dark Lady\'s army.',15595),
(24976,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent work, $N.  Now comes the fun part.',15595),
(24977,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'By the Light!  Finally some food!  Sweet, sweet pumpkin....',15595),
(24978,396,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve the makings of a mighty $c, $r.  I heard the cries of those humans from all the way over here.  Perhaps soon we will be rid of this human blight.',15595),
(24979,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The Scarlet Crusade takes no prisoners.  That they would do so with this young woman... curious.$b$bThe powers that you describe are even more curious.  She passed through the bars of her prison and killed her captor?  Why hadn\'t she done that in the first place?',15595),
(24980,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Most excellent, $c.  Your skill in the art of combat is undeniable.',15595),
(24981,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It sounds like we\'ll have to keep our eyes out for this Voss character.  I don\'t expect any Forsaken to receive a reward if we capture her... I\'m just worried she\'ll eventually turn against us.',0),
(24982,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Yes, I\'m Brill\'s local magistrate, reporting directly to the Dark Lady.  Impress me, and you may end up meeting the Banshee Queen herself.  Now, onto your first task...',15595),
(24983,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Magistrate Sevren wants a report?  Very well: the defenders at The Bulwark are holding the majority of the Scourge at bay, but some do slip through on occasion.$B$BWe have seen sporadic Scourge activity east of this station, with a concentration around the Balnir Farmstead.',15595),
(24988,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I appreciate your efforts, $N.  May Sylvanas recognize your bravery one day. . . .',15595),
(24989,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It is troubling to hear of the Scourge slipping past the Bulwark.  Even now, they are ceaseless in their assaults.$B$BBut we will not give in.  The Lich King is dead; we will not be taken again!',15595),
(24990,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You have done well, $N and I thank you for your efforts.',15595),
(24991,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Holland?  He\'s an amateur.  You don\'t need a fancy two-story apothecarium to make plague... you need love.  And maybe some good assistants.$b$bLet me show you how plague is REALLY made.',15595),
(24992,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hmm... yes, that makes sense.  Since the worgen have come streaming out of Gilneas, I knew it would only be a matter of time before they arrived here in Tirisfal.',0),
(24993,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'To think, they\'ve been right under our noses!  I\'ll put my deathguards on alert... this will NOT happen again.',0),
(24994,1,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, my doom weed. Excellent!$B$B<Apothecary Jerrod rubs his hands together greedily.>$B$BThese will come in quite handy. You\'ve done me, uh, the Lady, a fine service today, $N. As promised, here is the reward that you deserve.',15595),
(24995,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The scales are perfect, $N. Exactly what I needed for this concoction.',15595),
(24996,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, a drink at last.  What matter of ale is this?  I\'m sure it\'s no Rhapsody Malt but I\'ll take anything to wet the old whistle at this point.',15595),
(24997,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Expertly done, $N.  The Scourge are mistaken if they think they can use those corpses against us, and the fluid you gathered from the Rot Hide slaves will be studied by my master.  It may have secrets we can use against them.',15595),
(24998,66,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent work!  Now if only I can convince Jerrod to let us move our operation into that shack...',15595),
(24999,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Did they run from you, $N?  Good.  This is better than killing them... if they live to tell the tale, then future generations of murlocs will learn to fear us.',15595),
(25000,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hey, you\'re tougher than you look. These terrortooth hides reflect arrows and turn axe-blades - they don\'t go down easy, but their hides are worth their weight in silver in these light-forsaken Barrens. Nice work.',0),
(25001,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'And that\'s a wrap! Nothing left here for us but sand. Good job, babe.$B$BWell, maybe I shouldn\'t be so hasty. Did you find anything in that ogre den?',0),
(25002,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'My supplies! Well, that showed some real initiative, $c. Those rap-saws or whatever they\'re called have torn lesser men to ribbons. Thank you!',0),
(25003,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Your actions struck a telling blow against the Scourge.  And your victory will not go unnoticed - not by the Forsaken, nor by our enemies.$B$BContinue the struggle as we all do, $N, and one day the Forsaken will have the dominion over Azeroth that they are owed!',15595),
(25004,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Your efforts are appreciated, $N.  I will not thank you for doing what is necessary, but I will remember your name.',15595),
(25005,396,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Devlin Agamand?  Is that him you carry in your sack there?  Ha!$b$bYes, I know what Coleman wants to try, and I want to try it too.  I hope you\'re prepared, $N.',15595),
(25006,1,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, how unfortunate.  Perhaps the Scourge\'s dominion over Devlin\'s mind remained too strong.  Or perhaps our methods are simply not strong enough.  It\'s also possible that Devlin was too simple-minded to comprehend what we were asking him.',15595),
(25007,274,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<The High Executor sizes you up.>$b$bNot much of a $c, are you?  Well, you will be when I\'m done with you.',15595),
(25008,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ooooo-oooh aye! The best Hecklefangs are the dead ones.',0),
(25009,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Your actions will slow down the Scarlet Crusade\'s advancement in Tirisfal quite a bit... hopefully for good.  But other threats loom.',15595),
(25010,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'As you look over the ruins of the camp, you hear a whisper behind you.$b$b<\"I could kill you right now if I wanted to.  You\'d better watch your step, $r.\">',15595),
(25011,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Sure, I\'ll give you a ride.  If High Executor Derrington asks for it, then technically I have to.',15595),
(25012,1,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Welcome back, $N.  I\'ve heard stories from the east.  Who would have thought that a young $r $c like you would have been the one to wipe out the last whimpering remnants of the Scarlet Crusade?',15595),
(25013,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, this venom will do perfectly, $N.  Everything else has been added to my concoction and boiled down.  Thank you, $c!',15595),
(25014,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You found that in the ogre den? That\'s...$B$B...nothing to get excited about, I\'m sure! I\'m sure it\'s just...a perfectly benign trinket...that I\'m going to give you precisely detailed instructions on exactly how to handle.$B$B<Megs drops her voice to a whisper.>$B$BKeep your voice down and don\'t wave that thing around.',0),
(25015,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Corporal Teegan nods as you deliver your report, then grasps the Bramblestaff with both hands.>\n\nSo, this is what the quilboar are using against us? Do you think they used these to create this jungle?',0),
(25017,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you, $C. We would be hard pressed to face such enemies without your assistance.',0),
(25018,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Of all the...you found this in an ogre den? Unthinkable. I\'m amazed they didn\'t try to smash it to pieces.$B$BWith any luck, $C, we\'ll be able to obtain even more fascinating antiquities here...if you\'re willing to help.',0),
(25019,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent. The less interference from the Alliance, the better.',0),
(25020,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you, $n. With that dealt with, we can focus our attentions fully on exploring the gateway.',0),
(25021,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Mazoga gathers the pile of blood in his hands and raises it to his mouth. It liquifies and pours gorily down his throat.>$B$BDey drink de blood, dey get de power. I drink dere blood...$B$B<Mazoga gives you a wide, blood-smeared grin.>',0),
(25022,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good work. Gaines passed through here not long ago on his way to Northwatch and a warm bath.\n\nThe mission wasn\'t a total loss, though. We\'ve learned a good deal about these quilboar and their leadership structure.\n\nNow we can handle things ... MY way.',0),
(25023,396,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I told you we would meet again, $n.$B$B<The Warchief gives you an appraising look.>$B$BUnfortunate that it\'s under such dire circumstances.',27602),
(25024,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I\'ve not seen a finer display of $c prowess.',27602),
(25025,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Mazoga grins as he takes the sword from you in both hands.>$B$BDidn\'t like ya much, eh? More in this world craves blood than just trolls, mon.$B$BLet\'s find the other blade...',0),
(25026,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Mazoga tilts his head back and inhales the clumps of mysterious material. His eyes flash.>$B$BPowerful stuff, mon... ah, if ya could see what I see now... mebbe you go try it yaself sometime.$B$BThe spirits call...',0),
(25027,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'...Torn limb from limb!? Well, I\'d almost feel bad but the burning hatred gets in the way. She got what she deserved.\n\n<Corporal Teegan takes the Bramblestaff and snaps it over his knee.>',0),
(25028,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, samples from different parts of the overgrowth? These will be immensely helpful, yes. Thank you, $c.',0),
(25029,396,396,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Revenge has a sweet taste, don\'t you think?  When you destroyed the Agamands, did you catch any hint of free will within them?  I hope so.  I hope they knew fear before they were smashed into oblivion.$B$BIt is a foolish hope, I know.  But it is a hope I foster nonetheless.',15595),
(25030,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Is this Dargol?  He was vicious even in life, with a temper that bit deep and a blade that bit deeper. Undeath has not done him any favors, though it suits his personality. Yes, this was certainly Dargol.  I can sense his malice, even from the remains you\'ve fetched. You have my thanks, $n. ',0),
(25031,396,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Argh!  Get back!  Oh, you\'re not Scourge, are you?$b$bThank the Banshee Queen that you\'re here.  I\'ve greatly underestimated how bad it\'s gotten up here.',15595),
(25032,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Mazoga? He\'s taken the sword? That filthy...$B$B<Trenton glowers for a moment.>$B$BAt least you escaped with your life. The Lasher\'s bite is a vicious one.',0),
(25034,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, $N! I\'ve been talking you up to the General here. Thank you again for saving my life.',0),
(25035,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Здорово, что ты с нами, $gбратишка:сестренка;.$B$BВ такие минуты начинаешь гордиться, что служишь Вол\'джину, и хочется шагнуть прямо навстречу опасности.',26365),
(25036,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'So, Paxton says there\'s no jungle in the Barrens? What do you call THIS!?\n\nI\'ve got a pile of supplies to move to the interior and my camp has been overrun by a forest that - I swear - grows by the hour!',0),
(25037,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oi! Tasty, mon. Thank ya for your great kindness, young one. Da spirits shall surely be regardin\' ya with great favor.',15595),
(25038,6,5,1,0,0,0,0,0,'What\'s this? Gloom weed?! I\'ve no need for gloom weed! That mindless mass of flesh is out there picking daisies and convincing the Lady knows how many dupes like you into doing the same. No offense.$b$bWe\'ll deal with the gloom weed later.  For now, we\'ve got other matters to discuss.',15595),
(25039,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hmm... yes, that makes sense.  Since the worgen have come streaming out of Gilneas, I knew it would only be a matter of time before they arrived here in Tirisfal.',0),
(25041,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Nice work! How was it? Did you enjoy the hunt?\n\nDid you run through tall grasses, the scent of your prey urging you forward, until you leapt at its throat, adrenaline surging as your slavering fangs... Well, something like that.',0),
(25042,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Sam\'s eyes bug out of his head as you slam the huge slabs of meat before him.>\n\nOh yeah... oh ... YES! I\'ll have mine raw. I suppose I can grill some up for the others... How would you like yours?',0),
(25043,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Very good. We may never drive the Horde completely from these lands, but with a strong presence we can undermine their will to fight.',0),
(25044,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'A \"Boarpocalypse,\" you say? These animals certainly have a unique idea of \"Single combat!\"\n\nNo matter, you\'ve done well. With the quilboar in chaos I should have no trouble convincing the field commanders to execute any strays they find scurrying about. The General need not know we\'ve stepped up the campaign... it\'s for the better.',0),
(25045,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Your report, $c?\n\n\n\nIncredible, $N! You\'re a real asset to the Alliance. I\'ll see to it that my men follow your example!',0),
(25046,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'From birth to grave to undeath, we all have our own path to follow.  Some are easier than others.  It sounds like this Voss girl has had a rough path so far.$b$bHopefully she ultimately chooses to join us and follow the Dark Lady.  With power like hers, we could do incredible things.$b$bBy the way, $N... excellent work out there.  If you\'re ever ready and willing, I may have some more work for you in the Plaguelands.',15595),
(25048,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Most of this looks just fine! How lucky!$B$BThe Steamwheedle goblins will be so happy to see their cargo back safe and sound. And here\'s a reward for your good deeds, of course!$B$BWe\'ve got lots of other stuff to do though! Busy busy!',0),
(25049,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh, it\'s going to be so much nicer around here now that they\'re gone!$B$BAt least until more show up. But thank you!',0),
(25050,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'That was great! It looks like most of the goblins we helped made it back here and didn\'t blow up. We really showed that goblin girl!$B$BHere\'s a special reward for you, $gmister:miss;.',0),
(25051,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is a great relief, $C. Thank you.',0),
(25052,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good job! We\'re really cleaning up around here!',0),
(25053,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Isn\'t that just so pretty to watch?',0),
(25054,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Fantastic! Gosh, this will make enough wire for an entire army.$B$BLucky us!',0),
(25055,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done $n. But for every element that is subdued another one takes it\'s place. The solution we have here is merely a stopgap. Hopefully my brethren in the Earthen Ring are making more headway.',0),
(25056,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Dithers, you\'ve done it again!  These are perfect.',15595),
(25057,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $N. Several of the looters have already crawled back, requesting clemency. I\'ll let them stew for a bit in the Northwatch brig.\n\nThank you for helping maintain discipline in the ranks. It is important for our army to be perceived as soldiers, not common bandits.',0),
(25058,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Score one for the goblins! Stupid dwarves and gnomes.',27602),
(25059,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What have you dug up for me? Hmm. Interesting. This notice from Orgrimmar indicates a change in Horde leadership is underway - I guess heads are going to roll after what we did to Taurajo.\n\nWhat\'s this? A death warrant for the General here! This is good to know... Very good to know...',0),
(25060,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Your reports of their behavior are truly disturbing...but also slightly amusing.$B$BIf only that Dreadshredder wench had escaped on these vessels instead...',0),
(25061,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I\'m amazed that Soothfancy was capable of following a simple set of instructions. And ones that required him to keep his foolish mouth silenced as well.$B$BIn addition, it is honestly good to see you again, $n. Now that I\'ve dropped the charade, you\'ll get to see how gnomes get things done around here.',0),
(25062,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Kelsey takes the journal and gingerly flips through it.>$B$BI\'m trying not to laugh. This is classic. They have no idea they\'re even on Kalimdor!$B$BThese later pages though...something more significant may be occuring here.',0),
(25063,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well, gosh, this day just keeps getting better and better! I may actually smile.$B$BWhen you\'re not looking. You\'ve seen enough of that already.',0),
(25064,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hey there, hon. Vol\'jin sent you? So sweet of him to be thinkin\' of me.$B$BI surely could use da help, but ya have a bit more walkin\' ahead of ya.',15595),
(25065,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $n. The contents of this chest are sure to advance Gnomeregan\'s knowledge base significantly. I believe you\'ve earned a reward.',0),
(25066,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'YES!',27602),
(25067,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'An impressive start. Be prepared for more.',0),
(25068,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Marvelous. To think the shapers of our world crafted these...',0),
(25069,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This chest lies undisturbed, sealed for thousands of years.',0),
(25070,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The chest now grinds open again, the rest of the antechamber fallen silent.',0),
(25072,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thanks for the help, this was really killin\' things here. Once you start losing men, you start losing manpower. And morale. And weapons. And the magazines you loaned to that one guy.$B$BYou know how it is.',0),
(25073,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Welcome, young $r. Ya come highly recommended, mon. It\'s nice ta finally be meetin\' ya in person. ',0),
(25074,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Have you heard? The General never made it!\n\nKilled in the field, like some kind of dog!',0),
(25075,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oohh look! A mostly complete exhaust manifold, a reciprocating junction box, a working counterweight slip differential ... you sure know your junk, $N.',0),
(25079,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Great! Set the keg down right here. I\'ll measure out some charges once I\'ve donned my full-body protective gear.',0),
(25080,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<The gizard shocks Mizzy as you hand it over, blasting her to the ground.>\n\nOh, OH! That\'s nasty! I love it!',0),
(25081,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Incredible work, $N! My men report a breakthrough. Their stronghold won\'t survive much longer...',0),
(25082,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'That oughta take care of our bug problem for a while - they\'ll be hard-pressed to tunnel their way outta that!',0),
(25084,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve my thanks, if not that of the entire Earthen Ring.\n\nMaybe someday we\'ll find a way to talk it out with these pigs, but we can\'t heal the land if we\'re dead in our sleep.',0),
(25085,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'That\'s a relief. Maybe the rest of \'em will keep to their own devices now. The less fighting around here, the better.',0),
(25086,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What? Little Logan thinks I might need protection?\n\nIt\'s me doing the protectin\'!\n\nThe quilboar here are poised to rampage. They\'ve choked off the entire south, and we\'re the only thing standing in their way.',0),
(25087,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<The General reads over the report, nodding in approval as he reads about the Battlescar.>\n\nQuite a name you\'re earning for yourself here in the Barrens, $N. But Roberts isn\'t going far enough. What we need is a decisive victory...',0),
(25089,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Those val\'kyr have been really busy resurrecting you newbies lately.  I\'ve already seen a couple dozen new bodies run down that hill since this morning.$b$bYou, however, are the most promising $c I\'ve seen today.',15595),
(25090,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done.  I enjoyed watching you smash those undead into rotting pulp!',15595),
(25091,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Marin sent you? I\'m appreciative of his help.$B$BI\'m here to seek out Sul\'thraze. If you wish to help, speak with Mazoga...he\'s been cooperative so far.',0),
(25092,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done $n. But for every element that is subdued another one takes it\'s place. The solution we have here is merely a stopgap. Hopefully my brethren in the Earthen Ring are making more headway.',0),
(25093,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you, $n. The spirits of the fallen can now be put to rest.',27602),
(25094,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Not bad. You\'ve got a ways to go, however.',0),
(25095,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Rather impressive. Few can bear to see a silithid reaver face to face, let alone defeat it.',0),
(25098,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Once again you have helped us to overcome our mutual enemy, the Alliance.$B$BNow it is time for us to help you.',27602),
(25099,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Of course you can borrow Bastia. That is, if she\'ll take you.$B$B<Kilag winks.>',27602),
(25100,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'$n?! Nice kitty.$B$BLook we don\'t have much time here. You might have noticed that the volcano is blowing?!',27602),
(25102,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I thought you might be responsible for them clouds of dust I saw to the east. Nice work! Them bulls ain\'t sissies.',0),
(25103,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'re with Megs, huh? Word is she\'s been pretty hell-bent on making nice with Noggenfogger.$B$BNot like I care. Are you ready to kill some bugs?',0),
(25104,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Father sent you? He worries too much. There\'s nothing here I can\'t handle...\n\nBut I\'d still appreciate the help.',0),
(25105,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve really saved my skin, $n. Thanks!',0),
(25106,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'My father would be proud of you, $N.\n\nNow, to get this flying machine up and about again...',0),
(25107,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is truly incredible. The hieroglyphs are undoubtedly titan, but the markings below it...$B$BSome of these characters resemble ancient Kaldorei writings. And you say the antechamber was covered in hieroglyphs?$B$BYou\'ve made a find more monumental than any riches, $n. Please, take whatever reward you prefer.',0),
(25108,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Marley nods grimly.>\n\nAye, it\'s for the best I suppose.',0),
(25109,6,0,0,0,1000,0,0,0,'<The assistant looks confused.>$B$BHuh... what? Who?',27602),
(25110,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Assistant Greely spots the Kaja\'Cola Zero-One in your hand and her eyes seem to come to life.>',27602),
(25111,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Alchemists pay through the nose for these things. Sure, maybe I tell some of them they\'re dragon parts, but that ain\'t my problem, right?',0),
(25112,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Nice going, kid. Didn\'t lose any fingers? Good, we can get some more work for you then.',0),
(25115,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Beautiful! We\'ll have these puppies shined up and ready to sell in no time.',0),
(25118,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I\'ll rest easier knowing one of those lumbering things won\'t be wandering into my bedroom at night... again.  Thanks much.',0),
(25120,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<The battered dwarf hangs limply from the cockpit. As you approach the burning wreckage, his eyes flutter open.>\n\n<Marley Twinbraid is still alive!>',0),
(25121,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hi there! The fun\'s already started!',0),
(25122,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I hate the Trade Prince, but you can\'t argue with the results of his methods. Kaja\'Cola Zero-One is a huge improvement over regular old Kaja\'Cola at half the calories and twice the ideas!',27602),
(25123,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Your soulstone has expired, Blastshadow!',27602),
(25125,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Looks a little rickety....',27602),
(25126,11,0,0,0,2000,0,0,0,'Hmmm, not bad, $n. But don\'t let it get to your head...you\'ll fight tougher than boars in your career.$b$bNonetheless, you\'ve proven yourself well, and your next trial will be against a considerably more dangerous opponent, so you\'ll need some extra protection.',20574),
(25127,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'There is an important lesson that you must take away from fighting scorpids. The smallest or largest of opponents can still send you to your doom. In fierce combat, any number of things can prove your downfall.$b$bI have no more to teach you, $n. You have done well, and I will watch your progress with interest.',20574),
(25128,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Hana\'zua groans in pain.>',20574),
(25129,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'My blow was not enough to kill him, but looking at the damage I inflicted gives me some small measure of pride. That small measure will be all I have to sustain myself if I die, and in that light, the short list of my life\'s accomplishments fills me with anger.',20574),
(25130,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'From your description of the beast, I believe you must be speaking of Sarkoth! It is no wonder that Hana\'zua was overtaken by it. Aid will be dispatched to him immediately, trouble yourself no more with Hana\'zua\'s plight.$b$bHowever, I must say, I am most impressed to hear that you brought Sarkoth to death. It is a feat to be proud of, $n. And that you would fight for a stranger\'s honor, while other tasks occupied your time, your own honor is heightened.',20574),
(25131,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You have done well, $n.$B$BAlthough the Vile Familiars were merely pets of the darker powers within the Burning Blade, your success against them foretells greater deeds ahead.',20574),
(25132,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You retrieved it!  Well done!$B$BYour efforts within the Burning Blade Coven are key in rooting out this cult in the Valley of Trials.  But I fear they have further aims in our land.$B$BWe have not seen the end of them.',20574),
(25133,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hm... your report comes at a bad time.  The Burning Blade is no longer seen here in Sen\'jin, but we will be vigilant in our efforts to prevent their return to the area. The orcs are friends of the Darkspear Trolls.  Honorable friends.  We want to help the orcs, but... we need help too. ',0),
(25134,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good, good.  Maybe they\'ll think twice before slacking next time!  Thanks for the help! ',0),
(25135,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Great, you got it!  Thanks a lot, $n.  This is my favorite pick!  Now if my peons ever finish chopping down these trees, maybe we can find a nice cave to mine!',20574),
(25136,1,1,4,0,0,0,0,0,'Wonderful, $n! As promised, here is your cactus apple surprise plus a little something extra.',20574),
(25138,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ahh, where to start... introductions!  I\'m Acrypha - the one who sent you that parchment - I\'ve spent the last several years in an Undercity library, my head in a book.  I learned everything I could about the arcane, and now I\'ve returned home to share it with grunts like yourself. Shall we begin? ',0),
(25139,1,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You learn quickly.',20574),
(25141,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You won\'t be sorry. The ability to capitalize on the opportunities created by previous attacks is one of our greatest strengths.',0),
(25143,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Very well. Now that you know how to speak with the elements, we will test your bond with them.',0),
(25145,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You appear to be a quick learner. ',0),
(25147,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You understand now? Good, let\'s try it out.',0),
(25149,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good.  Now we practice. ',0),
(25151,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Marley\'s eyes sparkle as you rush toward him with the ale. He grasps the mug in both of his shaking hands and upends it, white foam spilling out over his blood-caked beard.>\n\nAh... that\'s the stuff. Ol\' Barkerstout... Thank you, friend.\n\nThat\'ll make this... a little easier.\n\n<Coughing one final time, he slumps over the shattered control console, the half-empty mug crashing to the ground and spilling its contents into the sand. His eyes glaze over.>\n\n<Marley Twinbraid is dead.>',0),
(25152,6,1,1,4,0,0,0,0,'Another one of Kaltunk\'s recruits, hm?$b$bA sorry state of affairs we find ourselves in if this is the best the Horde can produce. No matter. By the time we think you\'re ready to leave the Valley, you\'ll be a proud warrior of the Horde.',20574),
(25153,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'re a legend, $N.\n\nThe other survivors and I will be telling the story of your deeds for years to come.',0),
(25154,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thanks! I\'m sure to beat out that Marith Lazuria in Orgrimmar with these! I can\'t wait to see the look in her beautiful eye when I give this to her.',0),
(25155,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Your work is as good as it is rumored to be!',0),
(25156,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thanks. Erm. Just set them over there. I need to figure out how to get my hand off of this jar�',0),
(25157,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It did what!? We\'re ruined! Hmm. Well, actually... Maybe the professor can find some other applications for it?',0),
(25158,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve really saved my skin, $n. Thanks!',0),
(25159,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It did what!? We\'re ruined! Hmm. Well, actually... Maybe the doctor can find some other applications for it?',0),
(25160,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thanks! I\'m sure to beat out that Isabela Jones in Stormwind with these! I can\'t wait to see the look in her beautiful eye when I give this to her.',0),
(25161,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Your work is as good as it is rumored to be!',0),
(25162,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thanks. Erm. Just set them over there. I need to figure out how to get my hand off of this jar�',0),
(25163,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<One smoldering corpse stands out amidst the carnage. The dead goblin clutches the schematics of the fortress in his lifeless hand...>\n\n<The Bilgewater Cartel goblins. They did this!>',0),
(25164,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I\'m glad you were here, mon.$B$BToshe be lookin\' like he wants to chase dem down. You should go help\'em.',0),
(25165,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is it!  The scorpid juju Bom\'bay been waitin\' for!  Now we gonna fix you right up, $c. You come back to Bom\'bay when you be needin\' a pickup.  Bom\'bay got the spells to fix ya! ',0),
(25166,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'He was controlling a sea giant? Fascinating. If we\'d managed to investigate further...$B$BOh, I mean, wow, that\'s totally crazy! But thank goodness he\'s gone, hooray! Mister Noggenfogger will be so pleased.$B$BHere\'s a nice big reward, you!',0),
(25167,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well, we\'ve stymied their efforts for now, but they\'re still here.  We\'ll have to press on, $n.',15595),
(25168,274,1,0,0,0,60,0,0,'A battle well-fought, $c, but I still have my doubts about our effectiveness.  These humans don\'t seem to be going anywhere.$b$bYou, however, have done more than could reasonably be asked of any loyal member of the Horde.  Thank you.',15595),
(25169,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good work, hero.  You done good for Sen\'jin today.  No... you done good for all of Durotar.',15595),
(25170,94,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ya mon, that\'s tha stuff.  Now we get the other jujus.',15595),
(25171,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'That troll wants us to send help?  Bah, he can forget it.  I\'ve got my own human problems to worry about, and even those are the least of my worries right now.$b$bSen\'jin Village is right next to Echo Isles and the Valley of Trials.  Old Gadrin should find plenty of youngbloods to help him with his human infestation.',15595),
(25172,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Executed with quickness and discretion.  A job well done.',20574),
(25173,66,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Word of your bravery travels fast, $c. Tales of your victory at Tiragarde Keep will be heralded in Orgrimmar.',15595),
(25174,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What... WHAT!?\n\nBael\'dun in ruins? Corpses everywhere - no. No!\n\n<You describe the evidence you found at the scene.>\n\nThe Bilgewater goblins, was it? They want a fight do they? We\'ll show \'em what it means to be a part of the Horde, we will. I\'ll fill the Battlescar with their corpses. I\'ll redden the dirt with their blood.\n\n<Twinbraid grabs you by the collar.>\n\nGoblins. Are going. To die!',0),
(25175,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<General Twinbraid hurls his axeblade into the dirt, his voice quiet but his body quivering with disbelief and rage.>\n\nThat was my boy, $N. My only boy.\n\nThey\'ve made it personal, $c. Personal.',0),
(25176,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'$G You brought me my treasure!  What a sweetheart!: About time you showed up.  Don\'t even think about stealing that treasure... it\'s worthless here in Kalimdor, anyhow.;',15595),
(25177,66,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The scent of the sea hangs about you, $N.  Your efforts may have purchased another day for Razor Hill.$b$bI will pass word of your deeds up my chain of command.  You have our gratitude.',15595),
(25178,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'$g You really know how to treat a girl, you know that?  If you ever need anything...: Well, I suppose you\'re not completely useless.  Now stay away from my men!;',15595),
(25179,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I\'ve already spoken with several orcs that have returned from the beach.  All of them told me that you were the one who saved them.$b$bYou\'ve done a noble task today, $N.  Lok\'tar ogar!  For the Horde!',15595),
(25180,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Why would Twilight\'s Hammer take an interest in these tablets? Brann himself wrote that he hardly knows their significance, although he did mention something about becoming one with the earth. I will need to confer with my fellow Explorer\'s League scholars to decipher these as soon as possible.$B$BThank you, $n. Without your aid, these tablets would\'ve fallen into enemy hands.',0),
(25181,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Why would Twilight\'s Hammer take an interest in these tablets? Their contents are a mystery to our most learned scholars and deciphering them will take some time. If Twilight\'s Hammer knows about these relics and desires them, what more are they plotting?$B$BWe are most fortunate that you protected them from capture, $n.',0),
(25182,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Dead? Good.\n\nLet word of this deed spread, and with it, terror.\n\nThe Horde will feel the consequences of their attack on Bael\'dun, and they\'ll rue the day they ever crossed us, $N.',0),
(25183,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<The explosives are armed and ready!>',0),
(25184,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'As we would say in the Tinker\'s Union, out of the heat-applied metallic cooking container and into the oxydizing, energetic mixture of reacting gases and solids!',27602),
(25185,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Twinbraid nods as you describe the destruction of the mine, but his eyes still burn with rage.>\n\nVery nice work, $N. I suppose there\'s some strategic value in depriving the Horde of those minerals, but I\'d have done it anyway just to crush those little green monstrosities.',0);
INSERT INTO `quest_offer_reward` VALUES
(25186,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'So our supplies aren\'t getting through? Hmmm. Honor\'s Stand just gets more and more isolated.\n\nStill, the defeat of Thunderwalk should send a signal to our foes that we mean to stay. Thank you, $N.',0),
(25187,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I see... so the trick is that you need to put the LITTLE end of the spyglass up to your eye.  I\'ll remember that piece of information.',15595),
(25188,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I used that trick you taught me with the spyglass, and I watched you running around down there.  Quite impressive!$b$bHow\'d you make the old woman fly, by the way?',15595),
(25189,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'My grandmother was a powerful shaman in her day.  I thought she had lost most of her powers in her old age, but I suppose some things stay with you forever.',15595),
(25190,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Raggaran appears to have calmed down a bit since your last encounter.>$b$bGood, good.  One step closer to eliminating those beady-eyed, basket-wearing, hog-nosed, two-toed...$b$b<Raggaran\'s anger is clearly rising again.>$b$b...hunchbacked, squealing, prickly... no-good... gnome-loving... GREEEAAAAGH!  Quilboar!',15595),
(25191,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What, what!? Can\'t you see we\'re under attack here!$B$B<Gimbleheart snatches the readouts from the survey craft, then stuffs them haphazardly into a duffel bag.>$B$BYes sure of course I\'ll give Nibb\'s findings careful study. Later. From the safety of the Eastern Kingdoms, if I have any say about it!',0),
(25192,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Again, Raggaran appears calmer.>$b$bYou\'ve done well, stranger.$b$bI\'m sorry you had to see me like that.  Thank you for killing the quilboar, but maybe you should leave before I fly into another one of my rages.',15595),
(25193,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you, $r.  I will get to work on the necklace right away.$b$bBefore Kron died, I had made this for him to wear.  I have no use for it now, but perhaps you might.',15595),
(25194,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I love all the little animals, mon.  I love the big ones, too.  I just hate to see you hurt them like that... but it\'s for the best.',15595),
(25195,1,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Something happened to Screamslash when the cataclysm hit, Zen\'Taji thinks.  He wasn\'t always so violent and irrational.$b$bThank you for your help, $N.  Zen\'Taji gonna get back to his studying now.',15595),
(25196,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'re the one who handled the Burning Blade to the south?  I\'ve got ears in all kinds of places, $g boy: my girl;, and word travels fast.',15595),
(25197,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve ventured all the way here from Honor\'s Stand? Excellent, we could use your experience here.$B$BThey may have breached the walls, but Northwatch isn\'t going down without a fight.',0),
(25200,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I can\'t say that I was ever much of a footbomb fan, but you\'re giving me an appreciation for the game!',27602),
(25201,273,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Yeah, these will do nicely. You did good, kid. I\'ll see to it that you get the best footbomb uniform ever made.$B$BIn the meantime, you\'ve got other bombs to drop on the Trade Prince\'s lackeys.',27602),
(25202,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'He got just what he deserved. There, there, don\'t cry. You\'ll find someone else that\'ll treat you right.$B$BHere, let me take that... we wouldn\'t want people to think that you\'re crazy.',0),
(25203,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'There\'s no two ways about it... he got exactly what he deserved.',27602),
(25204,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'All of the lights and indicators on the control panel are going crazy!',27602),
(25205,1,6,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The moral of the story: hasty, lazy actions have ruinous results.  We mustn\'t take shortcuts... we must work for our rewards.  I\'ve been trying to tell this story to the \"Enforcer\", but I fear his Hellscream-worshipping skull is a little bit too thick.',15595),
(25206,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'See?  The shaman\'s tales are nothing but that... a youngling\'s bedtime stories.  The new Horde takes what it wants, and doesn\'t waste time with such frivolity.$b$bIf you get a chance, I recommend you tell Shin... and those like him... not to waste any more of your time.',15595),
(25207,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I felt the heat from the explosions all the way over here!',27602),
(25208,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'re back. What did Estulan say?',0),
(25209,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You have proven yourself to be a trustworthy and dependable ally, $n.',0),
(25210,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I thank you, $n. I will study the horns, but the situation has become even more dire since you left.',0),
(25211,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'That\'ll show \'em! Nice work!',0),
(25212,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Fantastic work!$B$BThe data I received shows the radiation levels are fully within safety range of our suits. That is excellent news!',0),
(25213,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I was wondering where you were!$B$BDon\'t worry, Hobart will get that footbomb uniform converted into the most Ultimate Footbomb Uniform ever!',27602),
(25214,6,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oops. Well, what goes up must eventually come down.',27602),
(25215,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It shouldn\'t take long to cleanse the water. Thank you for your help.',0),
(25216,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Another fan of the Great Sambino! Come all this way for an autograph perhaps? I\'m far too busy to be signing anything... move along now.',0),
(25217,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Another sample. Brilliant! The rocky riches of the sea shall soon be mine!',0),
(25218,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ya know, I should have given you a weight belt so that you wouldn\'t just float away, air balloon and all. Lucky for me you came down here with armor and all! Hah!',0),
(25219,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you. Seriously. If I would have had to endure another shipwreckee laughing at me, I swear I would have gored someone.$B$BI\'ll let you know if I come up with anything.',0),
(25220,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you, $C. There are still much bigger predators we\'ll have to keep an eye out for, but this will at least give us a bit of peace of mind around the cave.',0),
(25221,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Swift work. Very impressive.$B$BThat Fathom-Lord got away... I don\'t see him anywhere. He\'s most certainly the key to finding our captured friends.$B$BI will hunt him down. He cannot stay hidden for long.',0),
(25222,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'A friendly face! Welcome!$B$BVery kind of you to come check on us. We\'re fine. A naga scouting force did find us, but I\'m pretty sure none escaped. We should be safe for now.',0),
(25223,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I suppose your abilities are... suitable.  Color me impressed.',27326),
(25224,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'So you managed to pass this part of the test without getting yourself eaten by Smolderos or being incinerated by the fire elementals?$B$BI suppose I should congratulate you on ascending the lowest rung of our ladder.$B$BWell... congratulations, recruit!',27326),
(25227,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Gail sent you?  Did... did she say anything about me?',15595),
(25228,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Torek reads over the scrolls you collected.>$B$BWhoever these people are, they really mean to gain a following. It looks like they\'re having quite a bit of success. They can\'t be allowed to incite the citizens of Ogrimmar to panic and hysteria. We must discourage interest in this group and learn as much about it as we can.',0),
(25229,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is the best group of potential pilots you could find?$B$BOkay, well, I\'ll see what I can do.  I\'ve been known to turn even the biggest pile of gnarled gears into a smooth-runnin\' fightin\' machine and I expect no less with this lot.$B$BWell, I guess it\'s time to work!',0),
(25230,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'These events disturb me greatly. My study of the antlers while you were gone has revealed little.$B$BWe must find some way to fix this...',0),
(25232,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is quite interesting.  These rites aren\'t all that different from the spells which are taught to Horde warlocks.  This merits further investigation!',15595),
(25233,273,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done! The chaos we sow back here will be felt up and down the chain of command.',20253),
(25234,1,273,1,0,0,0,0,0,'\'<Jadi kicks open one of the crates and picks up a curved dagger within. She immediately winces in pain.>$B$BAugh! Cursed - this metal is cursed - it bites!$B$B<When the dagger falls to the ground, it shatters, as if made of brittle glass.>$B$BWhat demented workmanship is this? $n, I\'\'ve never fought any foe like this before.\'',20253),
(25235,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I saw you drop a few of them from here. Nice work.$B$BHere\'s your reward, on behalf of the Night Watch.',0),
(25236,1,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The electricity was only one of the dangers.  If those carcasses rot too long under the water, that entire source becomes undrinkable.$b$bWell done, $c.',15595),
(25237,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you once again, $n. I will prepare these for our final task.',0),
(25239,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You continue to prove yourself, $n. Accept this, not as a gift, but as a tool for the fight against the Scourge.',0),
(25240,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You continue to prove yourself, $n. Accept this, not as a gift, but as a tool for the fight against the Scourge.',0),
(25241,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The spirits of these guardians will return in time, $n. You\'ve freed them to move on in nature\'s cycle.$B$BNow it falls to us to make sure that cycle is free of corruption and needless suffering.',0),
(25242,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You are a true champion of our cause, $n. None can claim to be more dedicated to the struggle than you.$B$BIt is rumored that the minions of the Scourge fear you more than they do the Lich King himself. You are might incarnate.$B$BAccept this humble gift as a reward for your many triumphs.',0),
(25243,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I\'m sure she deserved it, $n. She should never have betrayed you like that.$B$BIt gives me the shivers to think that she might have kissed that monster, the Trade Prince!',27602),
(25244,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Serves her right for stealing your man in the first place.',0),
(25246,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'May you find what you\'re looking for, $gbrother:sister;.',0),
(25247,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'May you find what you\'re looking for, $gbrother:sister;.',0),
(25248,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'May you find what you\'re looking for, $gbrother:sister;.',0),
(25249,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'May you find what you\'re looking for, $gbrother:sister;.',0),
(25250,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The corruption has been stemmed! The forest can begin to heal now.$B$BMay you have the blessing of the Earth Mother wherever you go, friend.',0),
(25251,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You did it! You did it!$B$BWe\'re saved, $n!',27602),
(25252,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent! Even these fools will soon know that to stand against the Horde means death.',0),
(25253,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Anton reads over the scrolls you collected.>$B$BWhoever put these leaflets together knows how to get attention and from the state of things in Old Town, there\'s no lack of interest. We must act before they can build a significant following in the city. I fear they\'ll use their influence to spread panic throughout the city, paralyzing us.$B$BWe\'ve got to get inside the organization and learn as much as possible.',0),
(25254,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $n. Now we must focus our efforts on discovering more about this cult and freeing the people they\'ve conned into joining.',0),
(25255,273,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'\'Thank you, $n. I worry that our actions here may be too little, too late, but nature always has a way of rebuilding itself that never ceases to amaze.\'',20253),
(25256,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Vek\'nag sent you?  Without telling you that I need wagon wheels, nails, and rations?  That idiot.',15595),
(25257,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I watched you fight out there.  How long you been a $c?$b$bYou\'re alright, kid.',15595),
(25258,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I\'m at a crossroads now, $N... you defeated him easily in combat, but then again, I did get him for free, and he\'s pretty cheap to feed.  Maybe we\'ll keep him around for a bit.',15595),
(25259,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Fine, here\'s the money... but you\'d better make yourself scarce before I reconsider my policy on keeping Horde slaves.',15595),
(25260,1,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I ask for an orb, and you bring half of the goblin\'s arm with you?  I like the way you work.$b$bTell you what... you\'ve already given me a hand.  Allow me to return the favor.',15595),
(25261,2,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Welcome, $N.  Word reached me of your coming, and of your exploits in Durotar.$B$BYou are a $c of growing skill and renown.$B$BStay on the pure path, and your future will be great indeed.',15595),
(25262,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good.  Hiding within these collars is the secret behind the Burning Blade.  And I will uncover that secret...',15595),
(25263,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, and where did you get this?  Good Margoz sent you to me, did he?$B$BWell, let me take a closer look...',15595),
(25264,6,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is not news to me.  While I appreciate your efforts, the Burning Blade will have to wait.  We have other matters to which we must attend.',15595),
(25265,15,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Lok\'tar! Victory, $n!',27602),
(25266,1,0,0,0,1000,0,0,0,'I know who sent you. He be giving you something to deliver ta me, yes?',27602),
(25267,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thrall had you deliver this?$B$B<The Warchief takes a step back, visibly shaken.>$B$BI understand the meaning of this all too well, goblin.$B$B<Garrosh points to Gobber.>$B$BThis smelly thing was caught unattended in the city and seems to recognize you.$B$BI have already put others of your kind to work in Azshara. Take it with you when you leave.$B$BFrom this day forward, you and your Bilgewater Cartel will serve the Horde!',0),
(25268,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'re here to rescue me, $c? Thank you!$B$BNo, no, don\'t worry about the cage for now. My life isn\'t important. We\'ve got to save the shrine, first.',0),
(25269,15,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Lok\'tar, $c! Don\'t worry about this cage - these animals will come to fear me before long.$B$BMy first priority is to clear this filth away from my beloved shrine.',20253),
(25270,1,273,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Takrik examines the incense.>$B$BDisgusting. This is like the incense we burn when we wish to commune with the spirits... but it\'s... befouled.',20253),
(25271,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Ian examines the incense.>$B$BAs I suspected. These reagents bear the marks of the Twilight\'s Hammer. And here, the name \"Lycanthoth.\" I believe these are used in a summoning ritual...',0),
(25272,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You were brave to face down Lycanthoth, $n. Like myself, he was a primal force of nature... but his origins were from a darker place.$B$BThose who birthed that beast reached deep into the blackness, channeling powers never intended for this world.$B$BCome, $c. Climb onto my back, and let us show these beasts the true face of ferocity!',20253),
(25273,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You were brave to face down Lycanthoth, $N. Like myself, he was a primal force of nature... but his origins were from a darker place.$B$BThose who birthed that beast reached deep into the blackness, channeling powers never intended for this world.$B$BCome, $c. Climb onto my back, and let us show these beasts the true face of ferocity!',0),
(25274,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent.  I\'ll do my best to alter these documents.',27326),
(25275,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'$n? The $n?!$B$B$B$BThe rumors are already flying about you. I don\'t know if I should be thankful or frightened that you\'re here. At least we don\'t have any volcanoes in Azshara!$B$BHonestly, I can\'t believe you\'re showing your face here... Trade Prince Gallywix has setup shop atop the mountain!',0),
(25276,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'$ndamus?  Let us hope your parents brought you into this world with more than just a ridiculous name.',27326),
(25277,4,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hah! So you really sent some heads rolling, did you?$B$BIt was said during the War of the Ancients that Lo\'Gosh fought demons for ten days solid. Hopefully you weren\'t fighting that long...',20253),
(25278,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You really cleared that place out, didn\'t you? Well done!$B$BThe night elves once told me a story about how Goldrinn fought and killed a dreadlord, even as three others clung to his flanks, burning his flesh. I wonder if you or I will ever have the strength to do the same?',0),
(25279,4,1,5,0,0,0,0,0,'$n, it was incredible! For a fleeting moment I saw Lo\'Gosh through the trees - a creature of both fury and light. My cage collapsed and the vandals melted like wax under the kiss of his claws, their screams and howls echoing through the valley... Was that your work?',20253),
(25280,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'$N, it was astounding! Goldrinn himself appeared to free us, his white fur bright like the summer moon. Our cages collapsed and the vandals melted like wax under the kiss of his claws. He was beautiful, $N. Beautiful!',0),
(25281,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'While you were away, I was able to revive some of the fallen soldiers.$b$bWe\'ll need every hand if we are to survive here.',15595),
(25282,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $n. Now we must focus our efforts on discovering more about this cult and freeing the people they\'ve conned into joining.',0),
(25283,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh my.  Their reactions were that different?$B$BNot completely what I was expecting, but I think I have a speech that will do.$B$BJust let me find where I put it...',0),
(25284,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good, good. It\'ll take them many sleepless nights to figure out where we came from and where we disappeared to after the kills...',0),
(25285,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'',0),
(25286,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Toby is all done with the speech? Let me see...$b<Reads the speech> Pumping pistons! What a fantastic speech! I knew Toby was a good writer, but this is perhaps the best he\'s ever written.$bI think it\'s time to get you out to the battle.',0),
(25287,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is the final draft, then?  Let me have a look...',0),
(25288,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Welcome, friend. We are honored that you have decided to embrace the truth and join us. Come, there will be more time to talk later and you have much to learn.',0),
(25290,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Welcome, friend. We are honored that you have decided to embrace the truth and join us. Come, there will be more time to talk later and you have much to learn.',0),
(25291,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You think you\'re ready for the next step then, $ndamus?$B$BLet\'s see what you\'re capable of.',27326),
(25292,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Alto clenches the bullet in his palm as you tell your story.>$B$BGann? Dead? I ... I should\'ve known. His temper... his recklessness. I knew someday it would get the better of him.$B$BBut it sounds as though you\'ve already gifted him with vengeance. Thank you, $n!$B$BTurn your attention now to Dustwallow. If the Alliance finishes their cursed road through here, all your victories in the Barrens may have been for nothing.',0),
(25293,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'So you found them? Why did the missing men and women not return with you?$B$B<You tell the blood guard about the responses you received.>$B$BWe cannot compel them to change their minds and return to their families. I will let the families know that the relatives have been found and that they are safe. After this cult is broken up, they will likely return to their normal lives.',0),
(25294,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent.  This little pup will grow to be strong and merciless like his father.',27326),
(25296,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent job, $n.  Or should I say: \"$n\"damus?$B$BGive me a minute to read these.',27326),
(25297,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<You dump out the current contents of the cauldron, instantly killing the surrounding plant life.>$B$B<The draught you brew in its place boils chunky and reeks of rotted cabbage. You turn your head aside and bottle it up.>',20253),
(25298,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent! Let\'s hope the damage wasn\'t permanent.$B$BJudging by the poor victims still in camp here, the Twilight\'s Hammer really messed with their heads.',20253),
(25299,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve succeeded, $ndamus.  You\'re ready for the next step.',27326),
(25300,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<You approach the Eye of Twilight. As your fingertips graze its luminescent surface, you are aware of a malignant presence peering back at you, searching your soul.>$B$B<Instinctively, you draw back.>',20253),
(25301,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<A heavy tome, bound in flesh, lies open on the table.>$B$B<The language - pictographic and scrawled in rust-colored ink - is undecipherable, but notes and translations are tucked within several pages. This must be what you\'re looking for.>',20253),
(25303,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Flush with the energies of the captured elementals, you stand before the Twilight Apocrypha. The pages turn of their own accord.>$B$B<Suddenly, you see what the Eye sees. It is yours to command!>',20253),
(25304,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'These foul things will be driven back into the sea. I hope you\'re ready.',0),
(25308,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent job, $n!  You\'ve outdone yourself this time.',27326),
(25309,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'re on the fast-track to success.  Let us hope you don\'t ruin your track record with such silly notions as compassion and humaneness.$B$BCome, then.  Let us discuss your future.',27326),
(25310,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent work, $ndamus.  We must show all would-be competitors that we are not ones to give up easily.',27326),
(25311,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Sharp as always.  You do not disappoint me.',27326),
(25312,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hello, yes? What? You? Oh, you\'re one of the ones I sent after the Eye of Twilight, aren\'t you?$B$BGood work, very good. I suppose that\'s a valuable lesson:$B$BNever to take orders from a big purple ball.',20253),
(25314,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent work, $n.  Our plan\'s almost come together.',27326),
(25315,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You.  You\'re clearly not with them.$B$BAn ally then?',27326),
(25316,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Ysera appears to be in some sort of trance.>',20253),
(25317,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve arrived just in time, $n.',20253),
(25319,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'\'You\'\'ve done well, $n.  But I fear the battle is far from over.\'',20253),
(25320,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Help has arrived at last!',20253),
(25321,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'\'I am thankful, $n.  I will deliver my findings to our people.\'',20253),
(25323,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'\'Well done, $n.  This will help us turn the tide against the enemy.\'',20253),
(25324,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The dragon might be right.  The Twilight\'s Hammer has breached our security and this is our most dangerous prisoner.',20253),
(25325,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'\'You did well, $n.  I will take Fandral to Moonglade myself.$B$BHis prison will be far enough from the battlefront there.\'',20253),
(25328,4,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Kristoff reaches down to snatch the key.>$B$BIt\'s about time!$B$B<He squirms in his bonds, trying to reach the padlock behind his back.>$B$B...Can I get a little help here?',20253),
(25329,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'We\'ve done it! Cho\'gall himself has been utterly humiliated by you. His minions are dead, the Gordok are scattered, and now all will know the might of the Horde! Lok\'tar, $n. You\'ve more than earned your reward.',0),
(25330,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent work, $ndamus.  I\'m having the servants you chose for me briefed on their new duties.',27326),
(25332,6,374,273,0,0,0,0,0,'Kristoff, Kristoff... Oh yes, I remember now. I recall sending him on what amounted to a suicide mission.$B$BHe survived? I suppose that means he failed.$B$BStill, you deserve at least some coin for the trouble.',20253),
(25333,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Welcome back from the battle! The Twilight\'s Hammer have been disgraced in the eyes of the Gordunni, and driven from Feralas.$B$BWe\'ve shown the glory of the Alliance in full force today! Be proud!',0),
(25334,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'We\'d all suspected da naga, but I knew nothin\' of the Twilight Cult bein\' beneath the waves. Somehow dey are corruptin\' and pervertin\' the elements, makin\' demselves into dese horrors.$B$BWe goin\' ta have to be fightin\' both of dese threats to stand a chance of bringin\' peace ta Vashj\'ir. We don\'t have da men ta do that yet.$B$BCome, $C, we got much ta do.',0),
(25336,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'As my master told me...$B$BUpon a violent death, the muisek of a creature may escape and seek revenge. Shrinking the creatures, as you did, $n, prevents the muisek from escaping. Now we may use it as we please!',0),
(25337,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Master always said \"after killing an animal, if we allowed the muisek to escape, it may take the form of an even greater creature.\" This is dangerous stuff. Thanks for helping me with my studies.',0),
(25338,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you, $n. This is my first time working with treant muisek...',0),
(25339,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you, $n. You have put an old tauren\'s mind at peace.',0),
(25340,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Now I know that Edana is truly dead. This heart, I will keep it in memory of what you did here for me, $n. Thank you.',0),
(25341,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done. Let me have a look at this.',0),
(25342,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What\'ve you got for me here? You said the Gordunni had this?$B$BDisgusting...',0),
(25343,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Now that you understand the master\'s plan, you must prepare yourself to play your part.',0),
(25344,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ahh, I can feel the whelp in there. Let\'s get him out and ask him some questions...',0),
(25345,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you, $n. Now the spiritual powers of the faerie dragon will be available to us.$B$BI hope you willing to perform another task for me.',0),
(25346,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Just imagine the possibilities of what we now possess, $n. Along with the materials that you have collected, I will be able to forever trap the muisek of these creatures into whatever I wish.',0),
(25347,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<You hand Blood Guard Torek the devices that the overseer gave you, explaining the cult\'s plans. Torek\'s eyes go wide.>$B$BCho\'Gall is in charge of the cult? There can be no question then, this is the work of the Twilight\'s Hammer! You won\'t be the only one they\'ve sent into the city to deploy these devices.',0),
(25348,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent work, $n. Twilight\'s Hammer will think twice before trying to turn our own people against us again. I\'m sure I\'m not the only one troubled by just how many citizens were taken in by their message. Times aren\'t exactly easy, but if you have no honor or loyalty, you have nothing.',0),
(25349,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I thank you, $n, but the tale of your hunt troubles me. There should not be so many.$B$BThe sickness is still spreading...',0),
(25350,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<The apprentice\'s body is cold. He has been dead for a while.>',19116),
(25351,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<The warchief listens as you tell of your investigation into the Twilight\'s Hammer plot to destroy Orgrimmar.>$B$BYou are a dutiful member of the Horde, $n. You have done well in bringing this news to me. I will personally see to it that our enemies get what they deserve!',0),
(25352,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You should\'ve seen the battle from here! Bodies were falling off of the cliff! Spectacular!',0),
(25353,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'So, it is true! You indeed carry lightning in your hands.$B$BYou are the chosen one, $N. You will be my champion, and carry my vengeance to realms where I cannot tread...',0),
(25354,1,66,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Impressive, $n. Very impressive.$B$BYou embody all of the strength of the wolf ancient, and possess the wisdom to use your powers well. I salute you.',20253),
(25355,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'So, it is true! You indeed carry lightning in your hands.$B$BYou are the chosen one, $n. You will be my champion, and carry my vengeance to realms where I cannot tread...',20253),
(25356,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Jawn sent you? Good! We need your help, now!',0),
(25357,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Let\'s hope your efforts prove to be enough of a diversion...',0),
(25358,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I trust we both know what\'s been going on inside these crates...$b$bThat\'s right... ferrrmenntation! Here y\'are. My personal secret recipe.$b$bYou wouldn\'t get this from any other guy!',0),
(25359,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I remember you. You were there when they attacked us back in the cave.$B$BGood to have you with me, $C. Ready for a little vengeance?',0),
(25360,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Does everything down here only come in jumbo size? Oooh! That\'s a thought. Maybe there are some hunky sea goblins around here somewhere.$B$BThanks, by the way.',0),
(25361,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Wonderful, $C! These will do nicely. There are enough here to make a cloak for Korrin, and possibly even more! Thank you.$B$BI hope the trip wasn\'t too dangerous? The area of Feralas is not known for being forgiving, but you\'ve obviously done well enough.$B$BThank you again, $C.',0),
(25362,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Traitors to the Horde and traitors to their own people...$B$BI guess they\'re not all bad. They\'ll make fine drinking flasks.',0),
(25363,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is proof of a good start, $n. Your skills as a soldier are to be commended.$B$BYou are not the only one I ask that task of. Many before you have fought them, and in times past, our efforts have kept them at bay. Recently though, their attempts to push northward into our area of influence have increased dramatically. Their attacks have also become more savage... almost as if they were desperate.$B$BI have a plan though, $n, that might settle things once and for all against them...',0),
(25364,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve done as I have asked, and for that I salute you.  Take this small reward as compensation for your efforts, $n.$B$BWith their numbers thinned and their leaders slain, the gnolls will think twice about storming the camp.  This doesn\'t conclude the issue at hand, however...$B$BThere must be some reason why the gnolls have been whipped into such a frenzied state.  Before they have a chance to regroup, I want to find out what is causing it.',0),
(25365,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Examining the map reveals it to be the battle plans that Hadoken Swiftstrider wants. Numerous arrows that perhaps represent troop movements are drawn on the map, though most seem to be headed toward the south rather than to the north where Camp Mojache lies.$B$BAnother section of the map has a picture of what you think is a large insect of some kind, with various tick marks under it. From the looks of the gnolls, it perhaps represents their losses against the unknown bugs...',0),
(25366,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, this is exactly what we needed.  While I am not so skilled at ciphering what most of the scrawling on this map is, I\'ve seen enough battle plans in my day to understand what is happening with the gnolls.  It looks like they are currently fighting a two front war.  One is with us... but it seems that their main energy has been against a foe to their south.$B$BThere\'s more at hand here than meets the eye.  Perhaps it is time to figure out who this other foe they face really is.',0),
(25367,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $c.  Though the extensiveness of the Zukk\'ash presence will not be thwarted with anything less than a full-scale invasion, you have bought us some time so we can devise a proper strategy.$B$BI will be sure to have these carapaces analyzed; we\'ll need to learn everything about them before we deal with what has unfortunately turned into a much larger issue than we had anticipated.',0),
(25368,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I\'m free...finally! Oh, it feels so good to be free...$B$BOh, you saw, didn\'t you?',0),
(25369,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Impressive, $c... most impressive!  If Stinglasher is indeed one of their strongest creatures, the study of the beast will prove to be quite valuable in time.  It\'s now my charge to make sure we defend ourselves long enough to take advantage of it.$B$BPlease accept this coin bounty as a token of the entire camp\'s thanks, $N.  Well done.',0),
(25370,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve done well, $n.  We cannot allow the Twilight\'s Hammer spies this close to the world tree!',20253),
(25371,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Amazing! You look exhausted. She must have really made you work for it.$B$BLife should be a lot easier down here going forward with a mount that swift at your beckoning. Congratulations, $n!',0),
(25372,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is the key, $n! With the seedlings you collected for me earlier, the animals you\'ve saved from around Hyjal, and the Heart of the Forest you\'ve just discovered, we can rejuvenate this land right from under the feet of Twilight\'s Hammer. Imagine their astonishment to see their work undone, as life triumphs over chaos...$B$BI will begin the ceremony at once!',27326),
(25373,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I thank you, $n, but there is more work to be done to keep the camp safe. Listen further.',0),
(25374,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I will be able to rest easy now, $n. You\'ve saved our camp from a terrible menace.',0),
(25375,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good, good. Let\'s hope the ogres are at least smart enough to realize we\'re sending a message!',0),
(25377,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve discovered lost treasure!$B$BYour mind reels at the thought of what else might be hidden in the depths of the sea.',0),
(25378,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve come.$B$BI am ashamed to ask this of you, $c, but I\'ve ran from him long enough. Taerar must be stopped.',0),
(25379,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It is done.$B$BThis land that has suffered so much can rest now.',0),
(25380,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $n. It might be awkward at first, but you will get used to advocating our beliefs in public. It is one way of remembering our obligation to bring the truth to others. We must save as many as we can.',0),
(25381,66,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'\'Thank you, $n. You\'\'ve given us the opportunity to try to reclaim the upper hand.\'',20253),
(25382,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Dead? Good!$B$BBut it seems there\'s still so much to be done... fires to quench... and the soil to heal...$B$BI hope you\'ll stay close and help us reclaim Hyjal!',20253),
(25383,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You are truly blessed by the Earth Mother, $n, to have the honor of fighting with the guardians of nature, and to also survive it.$B$BKnow that you have kept safe every living soul in this camp, and possibly this entire forest. Take these gifts with my deepest thanks.',0),
(25385,4,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Squueeeee!$B$BDid the nice $gMr.:Mrs.; $c pull you from the flames, little friend? You\'re safe now!$B$BHooray!',20253),
(25386,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve been tussling with drakes, eh?$B$BI like it. We need someone who can pull their own weight around here. Are you ready to fight for the Horde?',0),
(25387,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I am thankful you\'ve come, $C. Our camp is beset by many perils, and yet we must tend to those fleeing the devastation of the cataclysm.$B$BIf there is to be any refuge here, you must help us.',0),
(25388,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Why, $n! What a surprise!$b$bIf anyone ever calls your character into question you be sure to send them my way.$b$bI\'ll tell anyone who\'ll listen that in my moment of need, you gave me a case of crabs...',0),
(25389,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh, my!$b$bThat\'s some of the biggest, juiciest tail I\'ve ever seen!',0),
(25390,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh, you\'ve found them! I was sure they were lost forever...$b$bHere you are, $n. I hope this is ample payment.',0),
(25391,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'As promised, you have your choice, $n. The muisek of the creatures has been forever sealed into the power of these weapons.$B$BYou may now wield their energy as your own. Use it well.',0),
(25392,1,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh yay! Happy little deer!$B$BNow they can grow up and have ADVENTURES.$B$BYou\'re swell.',20253),
(25393,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Curses! We had to fall back. But Thermaplugg\'s lost, and he knows it... he\'s only bought himself time. We hold the surface, and when the radiation clears we\'ll assault and recapture Gnomeregan with a force twice this size.',0),
(25394,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This development worries me greatly. This has happened before...',0),
(25395,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank the Makers! It\'s downright pristine. Those orcs couldn\'t figure out the tap-lock, it seems...and couldn\'t hack through the mastercraft work of Ironforge\'s keg-crafters with their crude weapons!',0),
(25396,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The mountain giants are precious allies of our race. We must stop this corruption before it claims any more creatures of the forest.',0),
(25397,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The spirits of these guardians will return in time, $n. You\'ve freed them to move on in nature\'s cycle.$B$BNow it falls to us to make sure that cycle is free of corruption and needless suffering.',0),
(25398,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Your bravery has seen us through! The Emerald Nightmare has been shut out from this land.$B$BThe fate of the dragon Taerar worries me...but there is much work still to be done. I cannot afford to dwell on it.',0),
(25399,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Your valor was mentioned in my briefings, $n. I commend you.',0),
(25400,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It sounds like there were more than we thought! Thank you for your brave work, $n.',0),
(25401,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Is that it? Let me see here...',0),
(25402,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ahh, the orb I mentioned before. A decent reason to disturb me.',0),
(25403,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, you\'ve brought him. Now I merely have to suffer the fate of speaking to him.',0),
(25404,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Very well, $r. I will help you mortals, even from within my bonds.$B$BBut don\'t sicken me by claiming it\'s my redemption. I do this for my own ends.$B$B<Blackhorn\'s sudden grin is unsettling.>',20253),
(25405,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I hear you, $r.$b$bI understand the urgency, but these men are in no condition to fight.',15595),
(25406,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Wonderful! Everything\'s going according to plan. Lady Shandris will be pleased.',0),
(25407,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Wisps have always lived in harmony with night elves, and we depend on them for many things. These little guys you sent back, for example, will be helping us with some new construction and repairs.$B$BReady for more?',0),
(25408,1,11,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Very good. Please crush the berries into a pulpy liquid. That\'s quite an aroma isn\'t it?$B$BNow now, don\'t gag. It\'s beneath you.',20253),
(25409,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'A properly trained squadron of hippogryph riders can take on nearly any opposing force. Feathermoon Stronghold will be much safer with these noble beasts on our side.',0),
(25410,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'They may not look it, but some treants grow to be ancient protectors. We could use a few more of those around here...',0),
(25411,2,6,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<The wretched creature before you speaks in a wavering voice, its body broken but briefly animated by Blackhorn\'s vile potion.>$B$BYes, master?',20253),
(25412,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Yes, yes! Show me the runes you discovered.$B$B\"Vol\'talo Thol\'embaar.\" That\'s the name of your real enemy.$B$BPresumably you\'re dealing with one of Ragnaros\'s generals, sent here to scorch the mountainside and pave the way for his conquest.$B$BI will show you how to crush him.',20253),
(25414,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'So you found them? Why did the missing men and women not return with you?$B$B<You tell the captain that they seemed determined to stay for various reasons.>$B$BThen we cannot force them to come home. I can only hope that in time, the cultists will realize the harm their actions have caused and decide to return to their normal lives.$B$BThank you for your efforts, $n. I will tell the families what you found.',0),
(25415,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $n. It might be awkward at first, but you will grow accustomed to advocating our beliefs in public. It is one way of remembering our obligation to bring the truth to others. We must offer hope to everyone, for we all face the end of this world together.',0),
(25416,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Now that you understand the master\'s plan, you must prepare to play your part in making it a reality.',0),
(25417,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<You hand Captain Anton the devices that the overseer gave you, explaining the cult\'s plans.>$B$BCho\'Gall is in charge of the cult? Then, it has to be Twilight\'s Hammer! We suspected that they would try to strike again, but no one knew what form the attack would take.$B$BYou\'ve done an excellent job uncovering this plot. Unfortunately, you won\'t be the only one they\'ve sent into the city to deploy these devices.',0),
(25418,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent work, $n. Twilight\'s Hammer will think twice before trying to turn our own people against us again.$B$BWhat worries me is how many citizens joined their movement without thinking about the cult\'s empty promises. Are times so dire that people will abandon the Light for promises of power and immortality?',0),
(25420,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good work, $C. We\'re that much closer to the secrets of Uldum.',0),
(25421,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is amazing. These hieroglyphs are undoubtedly titan, but the markings below it...$B$BIf I had to hope, this is the same passage written over and over again in an entire assortment of ancient languages. We might be able to use this to decipher the hieroglyphs! If the antechamber was covered in them as you say, who knows what else we\'ll learn.$B$BI\'d like to grant you a fine reward, $n. We\'ve made the find of the century!',0),
(25422,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you! Thank you...$B$BI feel much better. With just a bit more...',0),
(25423,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You can feel their anguish, can\'t you?$B$BMy poor friends. At least we can use you to fix things...',0),
(25424,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'\'This development is troubling, $n.  We must act swiftly.\'',20253),
(25425,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<The king\'s face takes on a look of concern, and then anger as you describe the Twilight\'s Hammer plot to destroy Stormwind.>$B$BHow dare they strike Stormwind? How dare they try to manipulate the people of this city against us and the Alliance! If not for your valor this day, $n, our city would not have discovered this Twilight\'s Hammer scheme. You are a true hero of Stormwind and the Alliance.',0),
(25426,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent work, $n. I didn\'t think those gnolls would give you much trouble.',0),
(25427,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Perfect. Any gnolls left will be simple prey, lost in the woods.$B$BHeh...here, soldier, take your reward before I get distracted. We\'ve got other threats to deal with.',0),
(25428,5,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'There it is! Such a trophy! Born in the fires of another plane...$B$BGo ahead, $r. Crush it. Crush his charcoal heart in your hands and let the winds scatter the ashes... yes, yes.',20253),
(25429,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'These are silithid after all...I wasn\'t sure, having never seen one in person. Gilneas had its problems, but at least we didn\'t have these monstrosities running around!',0),
(25430,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'My duties are here, viewing the enemy\'s movement from above, commanding our armies where they\'re needed.$B$BYour aid would be most welcome.',20253),
(25431,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $n! You\'re proving very valuable to securing this area for the Alliance.',0),
(25432,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It\'s good to see you back. We\'ve learned more about the ogre situation.',0),
(25433,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done once again, $n. Yet another threat removed from Feralas.',0),
(25434,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good work, and good riddance. I hope we never have to see another ogre here again!',0),
(25436,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I didn\'t want to scare you, but this is a grave situation. If the portal at Dream Bough was sealed, and the corruption is still spreading...',0),
(25437,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve come.$B$BI am ashamed to ask this of you, $c, but I\'ve ran from him long enough. Taerar must be stopped.',0),
(25438,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'To be drawn into a fight between dragons...I don\'t know if you\'re blessed or cursed.$B$BLady Shandris has heard of all you\'ve done, and has personally sent this reward for your bravery. I\'m glad you came back in one piece to receive it.',0),
(25439,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good to have a real warrior at my side. Too often, my shaman brethren can\'t seem to stomach the work.',0),
(25440,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'And with this, hopefully their attacks on us will calm for a while.',0),
(25441,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Too often, we are mistaken for druidic types. Perhaps that\'s true for some shaman, but do not let yourself be plagued by the ignorant belief that we are always peaceful.$B$BNothing about what I do is harmonious. I command the elements to my will. There is nothing offered in return. I would have it no other way.',0),
(25442,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What is this? A pearl? Much more I think.$B$BThis is exactly what I was looking for, thank you for bringing it to me.',0),
(25443,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Yes, yes! Show me the runes you discovered.$B$B\"Vol\'talo Thol\'embaar.\" That\'s the name of your real enemy.$B$BPresumably you\'re dealing with one of Ragnaros\'s generals, sent here to scorch the mountainside and pave the way for his conquest.$B$BI will show you how to crush him.',0),
(25444,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'These be enough for me purposes. Now comes de hard part.',0),
(25445,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'$n, you\'d be a mighty warrior and a fierce commrade to da Darkspear trolls.  De Echo Isles are OURS now and we couldn\'ta done it wit\'out ya.$B$BTake dis cloak. Wear it wit pride.  You\'d be a member of da tribe now!$B$BIn no time, da trolls will have a home again and we have you to thank for dat.',0),
(25446,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I\'m already beginnin\' to see what de frogs are seein\'. Ya done it perfectly, $N. Now Vol\'jin and I will see what Zalazane be plannin\'.',0),
(25447,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'At the very least, these creatures\' suffering has ended. Let us hope their sacrifice will bring a stop to further pain.',0),
(25448,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you, $c. That\'s one less distraction for me.',0),
(25449,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Did you stop and examine the texture of these hides?  Properly treated, these hides could very well be stronger than iron.  Not many people know about these hides, and that in combination with the vast treating solutions I know will allow me to potentially make items with a true mark of quality... thanks to you, of course!$B$BAnd now, please choose from what I am able to offer you for your service!',0),
(25450,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent, excellent!  These are going to work out incredibly well - I can already tell that they\'re going to be much harder when properly cured.$B$BThanks again for your help $N.  Here - please take one of my latest creations.',0),
(25451,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Incredible! You may have found the granddaddy of all yeti hides with this!$B$BYou better believe I\'ll pay you for it. I normally don\'t pay that much for a single hide, but I\'m pretty sure I can make something special from it. Thanks for thinking of me on this, $n!',0),
(25452,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, excellent! These hides, when given a special treatment, are as resilient as iron I tell you! It will take many tries in order to get the right mix down for the tanning, but I am confident they will bring my mark of quality to the next level.$B$BAs for you, $n... your assistance has proven invaluable to me. Please take your choice from these items I have crafted.',0),
(25453,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent, excellent! These are going to work out incredibly well - I can already tell that they\'re going to be much harder when properly cured.$B$BThanks again for your aid, $n. Here - please take one of my latest creations.',0),
(25454,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is an incredible find! I believe this is the finest yeti hide specimen I have ever seen!$B$BIndeed, this is certainly worthy of an appropriate bounty. I normally don\'t pay that much for a single hide, but I\'m confident I can make something special from it. Thanks for thinking of me on this, $n!',0),
(25456,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Sam\'s in one piece then? And his poor assistant Felice? Good to hear.$B$BI hope that one day he\'ll learn to respect the elements as more than just a tool.',0),
(25458,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good riddance to foul creatures. May the naga slither back into the sea and never return.$B$BYou\'ve proven yourself on the battlefield, $n. I would ask more assistance of you in defending our lands here.',0),
(25459,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well that\'s a load off my mind.$b$bThank you again, $c.',0),
(25460,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I thank you, $n.  Your fighting prowess is admirable.  You will be crucial to putting a halt to the elemental onslaught.',20253),
(25461,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ya found some good ones. I be trainin\' them hard and we won\'t stop until we\'ve driven Zalazane from our islands.',0),
(25462,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'\'I thank you, $n. Those little bears are shaken up but they\'\'ll survive.$B$BAt least the ones that hit the mat.\'',20253),
(25463,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good to see you here. Estulan is being...difficult. We\'re going to have to deal with these ogres for Lady Shandris on our own until he decides to deal with us.',0),
(25464,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'\'Well done, $n.  We cannot afford to lose any further ground in Hyjal.$B$BBy stopping Baron Geddon we will have dealt a huge blow to the enemy.\'',20253),
(25465,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Splendifimous!  Not only am I glad to see that you\'ve returned with the residue, but also with all your major appendages intact!  That is, well, there was never any danger in using the Ultra-Shrinker, now was there!$B$BI do appreciate your effort on my behalf, $N.  Truly, you are a friend to goblins everywhere.  Accept this as a token of my appreciation!',0),
(25466,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Scrumdillyriffic!  These cores will keep me working for some time.  Add to that the benefit of there now being fewer elementals along the coast, and I might no longer cry myself to sleep at the prospect of having set up shop in perhaps the worst place imaginable!$B$BThank you, $N, for your efforts on my behalf.  While it certainly straps me financially to do this, allow me to show you some gratitude you may understand and appreciate... loot!',0),
(25467,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The satisfying sound of a chest unlocking is followed by the sight of once-hidden treasure.',0),
(25468,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Aren\'t they adorable? The babies are even cuter.',0),
(25469,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent!$B$B$n, you\'ve helped bolster our forces here, and you\'ve saved many of these forest creatures from the Horde as well. With our army now ready, Feathermoon will stand against all threats, Horde or otherwise!$B$BOn behalf of Lady Feathermoon, I\'d like to award you with this weapon, fit for a Sentinel.',0),
(25470,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Vanira\'s frogs be tellin\' de truth, den? Dis tiger be a druid and an ally? We couldn\'t be hopin\' for a better outcome. Dis be a good omen for de coming battle.',0),
(25471,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ello, mon! You look a bit more capable then most of dem coming through here.$B$BCome rest a bit. Make yaself at home.',0),
(25472,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'\'Excellent, $n.  This will be a great weapon against the enemy forces.\'',20253),
(25473,1,25,0,0,0,1000,0,0,'Just so you know, you\'ll find Kaja\'Cola all over town. It\'s the Bilgewater Cartel\'s best-selling product of all time!$B$BJust remember, image is everything if we\'re going to get you promoted to Trade $g Prince : Princess;! No, wait, profits are everything! Explosions are a close second! Then, image!',15595),
(25475,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You place the egg... distress beacon... inside the chicken... homing robot.$B$BHums and whirs are heard from inside the robot as it struggles to stand up.  After the robot comes to life, Oglethorpe\'s voice is heard once more, but now from inside the robot:$B$B\"OOX-22/FE is working at least, but it needs major repairs!  It is much too heavy for you to carry it... but I think I have an idea.  Are you up for watching over it some more?\"',0),
(25476,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh, YOU\'RE the great savior of OOX-22/FE! I cannot even begin to express my thanks for your assistance! My homing robot series needs more development, but your recovery has saved me countless hours of extra rebuilding time, as well as many gold pieces in manufacture costs!$B$BPlease, take your choice of any of these items I have. Thank you again for your generous assistance $n, my robots and I are in your debt!',0),
(25477,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'How unfortunate...$b$bWell, all things considered, it is good to see that you made it back unharmed.',0),
(25478,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Nyse sent you? Good! We need your help, now!',0),
(25479,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thyssiana sent you? Good! We need your help, now!',19116),
(25480,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I will take de spirits\' advice to heart. Wit\' dem behind us and de power of de ancient loas of de Darkspear Tribe, we be ready to reclaim what\'s ours!',0),
(25481,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Falfindel Waywarder sent you? Good! We need your help, now!',0),
(25486,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'A boat? Yes, you can have this last one.',0),
(25487,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You want a canoe to go out to the salt flats? But, surely the race track has been destroyed?!$B$BNonetheless, for your bravery, you will have the last one!',0),
(25488,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'YES?! Do you see me interrupting your fascinating argument?$B$BNo... no, please, go ahead. I\'m sure that your interruption is about something very important. More important than dealing with the survival of everyone here, in fact.$B$B<Fizzle taps his foot impatiently.>',19116),
(25489,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Heya, kid, I\'ll be right with ya. Just gotta shut this gnome twerp up first.',0),
(25490,273,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Very good. The Twilight\'s Hammer must be sent the message that we will never give up.',20253),
(25491,273,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'\'<The Arch Druid inspects the seedlings.>$B$BThese seedlings have survived an apocalypse. Even a handful hold great power. Life always replenishes itself, often stronger than before.$B$BOnce the way is clear, we will use these to perform a miracle on this mountain, $n. You will see.\'',20253),
(25492,273,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'\'Good work, $n. There\'\'s a chance the forest will recover from this yet.$B$BNow, there\'\'s something else I need you to take care of for me...\'',20253),
(25493,1,273,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Very good. We will need these to act as bait while they are still warm.$B$BHere is my plan...',20253),
(25494,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent!  Our pup is ready for a fight.',27326),
(25495,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'At last, everythin\' be ready. Now, we show Zalazane what happen to dose who defy de Darkspears!',0),
(25496,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'That\'s how it\'s done!',27326),
(25499,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh.  You\'re still alive.$B$BNot bad.',27326),
(25500,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is the speech from Toby? Fantastic!$bRecruit, you\'ve done all we could possibly ask for and the Gnomeregan Army thanks you!$bWe\'ve got a strike team heading to Gnomeregan now and that wouldn\'t have been possible without your assistance. For all of your help, we\'d like you to join the Gnomeregan Reserves!$bIt doesn\'t pay very well, but you do get this snazzy helmet. Hang on to that, you might need it someday!',0),
(25502,4,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'That\'s good! Between your work and the work of a few others, that valley is secure from a counter-attack.$B$BI\'ve done all I can. It\'s all up to you and the Arch Druid now.',20253),
(25503,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This item was highly prized by the local gilblin population - even coveted by King Gurboggle, himself!',0),
(25504,6,5,0,0,0,1000,0,0,'<Jinky eyes the list of parts and spits!>$B$BI don\'t have even half of that stuff!',19116),
(25505,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Heya, pal, mind if I take a look at that list?$B$B<Razzeric nearly spits!>$B$BWhat\'s Pozzik thinking? He knows that I don\'t have even half of that stuff!',0),
(25507,1,273,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<The Arch Druid takes the shell from you with surprising reverence.>$B$BNemesis is an instrument of evil, but he was forged from a shell fragment of the true ancient.$B$BWe will exploit this connection.',20253),
(25509,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Very well.  You\'re at least competent enough to figure out which way the pointy end of the pick goes.',27326),
(25510,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'$R.$B$BThis tongue. Is not yours.$B$BWhat do you want ... tormentor?',20253),
(25513,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Fantastic. I might challenge you to a duel myself someday.',0),
(25514,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Tortolla quivers and shakes debris free from his great back.>$B$BYou...$BAre not like the others.$B$BI am free once again.$B$BThe others...$BWill pay.',20253),
(25515,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This\'ll do for a start.',19116),
(25516,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is a great start!',0),
(25517,71,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'That\'s the spirit! You\'re a real credit to the Alliance!$B$BYou know, you can go back in there and do that anytime you feel like it. I highly encourage you to do so!',19116),
(25518,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Yes! You\'re a real credit to the Horde!$B$BYou know, you can go back in there and do that anytime you feel like it. I highly encourage you to do so!',0),
(25519,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'$R.$BYou are not like the others.$B$BBraver. Stronger.$BA part of this world...$B    and not the shadow that came before.$B$BThank you.',20253),
(25520,1,273,0,0,0,0,0,0,'\'$n!$B$BYou were able to earn the ancient\'\'s trust?$B$BWonderful! We are one step closer to taking back this mountain...\'',20253),
(25521,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh thank you, thank you! I know a bit of alchemy, I\'m not totally useless. Here goes...',0),
(25522,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I can\'t believe it! You\'re amazing! Here, please, take your reward, take anything you want! I\'ve gotta save Chelsea!',0),
(25523,4,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done! How does it feel?$B$BIt is challenging to master flight in this burning wasteland, but it is the only way.$B$BI hope you\'re ready for battle, $n...',27326),
(25524,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank goodness! Now, just a little shove....',19116),
(25525,66,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Spectacular flying, $n! Their screeches of anguish echoed about this light-forsaken cavern.$B$BBut our work is not yet finished...',27326),
(25526,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank goodness! Now, just a little shove....',0),
(25531,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You have my thanks, $n.',27326),
(25532,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'One problem down. Now to deal with the greater threat!',19116),
(25534,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Nice work, kid. Any close calls? Did you get grazed?$B$BNo? Good, because we\'ve got more fish to fry here.',0),
(25535,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'More help! Superb! We can certainly use it, I\'ll tell you that much.',0),
(25536,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you for stepping up to take care of this, $C. I know there are a lot of concerns swarming us right now, but maintaining the safety of the survivors is paramount.',0),
(25537,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Superb! Chemicals abound!$B$BMy instantaneous chemical synthesizer is already pre-tested and prepared. Your deployment compound shall be ready in the blink of an eye!',0),
(25538,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done my odorific associate. You are both swift and assiduous, if I do say so myself. May your future travels be rampant with inspiration and opulence.',0),
(25539,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, indeed. This is an entirely unshameful amount of clams to have gathered. The survivors back at the cave will surely be grateful.',0),
(25540,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is wonderful. I will begin cooking them immediately. It is good to know that of our many fears, starvation shall no longer need to be one of them.$B$BI imagine the Admiral will have much work for you. Let me trouble you no further for a while.',0),
(25541,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Nice! Remember, gold is gold, no matter who\'s mouth, nose, or otherwise it\'s been in.$B$BIt\'s all perfectly sanitary after being melted down anyway. Or at least wiped off.',0),
(25542,4,17,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You did it! You did it!$B$B<Jinky grabs you and gives you a big smooch on the cheek! She then regains her dignity and smooths her clothes.>$B$BThanks for saving my Speedbarge, Captain $n.',19116),
(25543,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You saved my Speedbarge!$B$B<Razzeric embraces you in a manly hug!>$B$BI can\'t begin to tell you how relieved I am, Captain $n!',0),
(25544,1,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,'By the wings of Aviana - you were born to fly, $n!$B$BQuickly, let\'s get back out there and hit them again...',27326),
(25545,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $C!$B$BThanks to you, my men will be ready to confront the enemy when they attack.',0),
(25546,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This should help relieve our exhaustion.$B$BAgain, we thank you.',0),
(25547,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'No time to address the troops now.$B$BJust as well. They know what must be done.',0),
(25548,66,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You did well, $n.  I\'ve a new target for you.',27326),
(25549,1,6,66,0,0,0,0,0,'You continue to prove your prowess, $n.  At this rate Hyjal might survive this ordeal after all.',27326),
(25550,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent work, $n.  We shall soon claim victory in Hyjal.$B$BIt has been an honor to fight along your side.',27326),
(25551,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hyjal has been saved, $n.  And it\'s all thanks to you.',27326),
(25552,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve done well, $n.  We will use this to draw out the Twilight matriarch.',27326),
(25553,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'That went... better than expected.',27326),
(25554,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'These foul books should not be allowed to exist.  Yet the information inside them is of vital importance.',27326),
(25555,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It is done.  Only the final step in your mission remains.',27326),
(25556,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Mazoga\'s ghost gives you a blood-smeared grin.>$B$BHow you doin\', mon?',0),
(25558,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The Earthen Ring has received my distress message and sent help - just in time it would seem.$B$BHopefully more can be sent soon. We are but few against a great many.',0),
(25559,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'That\'ll teach the Horde twofold! Don\'t mess with dwarven history, and don\'t send a bunch of frail couch-dwellers to do your fighting!',0),
(25560,1,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,'A decisive blow! ',27326),
(25561,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You did it! You did it!$B$B<Jinky grabs you and gives you a big smooch on the cheek! She then regains her dignity and smooths her clothes.>$B$BThanks for saving my Speedbarge, Captain $n.',0),
(25562,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You saved my Speedbarge!$B$B<Razzeric embraces you in a manly hug!>$B$BI can\'t begin to tell you how relieved I am, Captain $n!',0),
(25563,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Not another one! $n, these devices have been springing up all around Azeroth. We know that they can instigate elemental disturbances in the area, including causing tears in the elemental planes.$B$BThe devices stink of Twilight\'s Hammer. The engravings covering the surface and the captured elemental essence implicate Cho\'gall and his minions are behind this.$B$BIf you find more of these, please bring them to me or one of my associates. We need to learn more about what\'s behind this attack!',0),
(25564,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Everything here seems to be in working order.',0),
(25565,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Would you take a look at these...not troll, not qiraji, just pure mystery waiting to be unlocked.$B$BThese aren\'t going anywhere now that they\'re safely in our hands. It\'s time to make our way into the ruins!',0),
(25566,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This chest lies undisturbed, sealed for thousands of years.',0),
(25567,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Not another one! $n, these devices have been springing up all around Azeroth. We know that they can instigate elemental disturbances in the area, including causing tears in the elemental planes.$B$BThe devices stink of Twilight\'s Hammer. The engravings covering the surface and the captured elemental essence implicate Cho\'gall and his minions are behind this.$B$BIf you find more of these, please bring them to me or one of my associates. We need to learn more about what\'s behind this attack!',0),
(25568,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Not another one! $n, these devices have been springing up all around Azeroth. We know that they can instigate elemental disturbances in the area, including causing tears in the elemental planes.$B$BThe devices stink of Twilight\'s Hammer. The engravings covering the surface and the captured elemental essence implicate Cho\'gall and his minions are behind this.$B$BIf you find more of these, please bring them to me or one of my associates. We need to learn more about what\'s behind this attack!',0),
(25569,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Not another one! $n, these devices have been springing up all around Azeroth. We know that they can instigate elemental disturbances in the area, including causing tears in the elemental planes.$B$BThe devices stink of Twilight\'s Hammer. The engravings covering the surface and the captured elemental essence implicate Cho\'gall and his minions are behind this.$B$BIf you find more of these, please bring them to me or one of my associates. We need to learn more about what\'s behind this attack!',0),
(25570,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Not another one! $n, these devices have been springing up all around Azeroth. We know that they can instigate elemental disturbances in the area, including causing tears in the elemental planes.$B$BThe devices stink of Twilight\'s Hammer. The engravings covering the surface and the captured elemental essence implicate Cho\'gall and his minions are behind this.$B$BIf you find more of these, please bring them to me or one of my associates. We need to learn more about what\'s behind this attack!',0),
(25571,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Yes, $n, this shard does explain the occurrence of the rifts. The elemental planes have been in chaos in Outland ever since Draenor was destroyed. These shards cause a weakness in the already damaged elemental planes and allow the elementals to cross over.$B$BWe\'re still collecting information on who or what is behind all of this. However, the more shards you bring me, the better prepared we will be to fight the elemental invasion here in Azeroth.',0),
(25572,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Not another one! $n, these devices have been springing up all around Azeroth. We know that they can instigate elemental disturbances in the area, including causing tears in the elemental planes.$B$BThe devices stink of Twilight\'s Hammer. The engravings covering the surface and the captured elemental essence implicate Cho\'gall and his minions are behind this.$B$BIf you find more of these, please bring them to me or one of my associates. We need to learn more about what\'s behind this attack!',0),
(25574,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent, $n.  That should put a stop to the attacks once we finish these elementals off.',20253),
(25575,1,273,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good, good. I like nothing more than to see the works of our enemy destroyed.',20253),
(25576,11,274,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Dead? Good. They sealed their fate when they threw their lot in with Ragnaros and his kingdom of flame.$B$BLeave their bodies down here to crumble into ash.',20253),
(25577,1,274,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Great work!$B$BThere was a time when adventurers would collect these cores in order to craft mediocre fire-resistant equipment. But for now, I\'m glad just to destroy these fiends once and for all.',20253),
(25578,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'\'Alysra\'\'s decision might not have been the wisest, $n.  Yet there is little time to worry about that now.$B$BI bring important discoveries from the Emerald Dream.\'',20253),
(25579,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent work, $C.$B$BI will get some of our own patrols out to make sure that no more naga get within sight of this cave. We should have the area secured within the hour.',0),
(25580,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $n, and just in time too. The Admiral just started sending more men out. Strong sword arms to be sure, but I doubt they possess quite the same awareness and finesse that you do.$B$BWe were lucky to have you here when things went south. I suspect you will have a large role to play in things to come as well.',0),
(25581,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you so much for taking this seriously.$B$BThis is some of the first definitive proof of other members of the Vashj family. Very interesting. And I\'d never even heard of either of the other two figures you mentioned until now.$B$BSo much of our history was lost during the sundering - it\'s exciting to have a chance at reclaiming some of it.',0),
(25582,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is good intel. You have a sharp eye, $C.$B$BIt sounds like the building tucked under the terrace at the far end of the ruins will make a suitable forward post. I will send some men immediately to start defensive preparations and we will reposition there as soon as possible.',0),
(25583,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Interesting indeed.$B$BThe remains you describe sound much like the sea vrykul we encountered in Northrend. I highly doubt we will be striking any alliances with their sort, no matter the cause. Still, this information may prove useful in the future.$B$BI will think on it further if time permits. Thank you for bringing it to my attention.',0),
(25584,6,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ysera sent you? Good! We need all the help we can get.$B$BWe\'ll never be able to recover the shrines to the ancients so long as Twilight\'s Hammer controls the roads. Somehow we\'ve got to stem the flood.',20253),
(25585,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'They\'re still shooting, but not nearly as much! Yeeeeeeeeeaaaaaaaaaaah!',19116),
(25586,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'They\'re still shooting, but not nearly as much! Yeeeeeeeeeaaaaaaaaaaah!',0),
(25587,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I cannot thank you enough, $r.$b$bI just hope this whole nightmare has a happy ending.',0),
(25588,66,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'That\'ll teach those scurvy dogs! You have my thanks, $n.',19116),
(25589,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'That\'ll teach those scurvy dogs! You have my thanks, $n.',0),
(25590,15,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hey! Get me out of here!',19116),
(25591,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Fantastic. I might challenge you to a duel myself someday.',0),
(25592,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You know what it is to carry yourself with honor, $c. You do Hellscream proud.',0),
(25593,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you, $c. You\'ve proven very useful.',0),
(25594,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Glad you know a quick buck when you see one. Pleasure doing business with you, $g buddy:gorgeous;.',0),
(25595,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Now to hold up my end of the bargain. I\'ll get this cooked and passed out immediately.$B$BYou and I will have to have a talk later. I\'m going to need help that these soldiers just can\'t offer.',0),
(25596,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hey! Get me out of here!',0),
(25597,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hey there.  I\'m glad to see they sent someone of your caliber for this operation.$B$BThis here\'s going to call for some subtlety.  We can\'t risk Commander Shadowsong getting killed.',27326),
(25598,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Where would we be without you, $r!$b$bI don\'t want to even imagine!',0),
(25599,6,5,1,0,0,0,0,0,'This is the tome we\'ve heard about?$B$B<Jordan hefts the stone slab into his arms and looks it over.>$B$BI see... I guess it\'s good that I can read some of the elemental script. I\'ll work on translating this. Meanwhile, there\'s one final problem to take care of.',20253),
(25600,4,5,273,0,0,0,0,0,'\'It is done! We\'\'ll seal this fiery hole up behind us and let the minions of the Twilight\'\'s Hammer discover the corpses we left behind. We couldn\'\'t have done it without you, $n!\'',20253),
(25601,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'There you are, $ndamus.  I\'ve been meaning to talk to you about something.$B$BI heard about the unfortunate incident that befell our poor friend, Okrog.$B$B<Mylva looks to her left, then her right.  She finally nods and shoots a sly wink in your direction.>$B$BYou might be a better pupil than I had thought.',27326),
(25602,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Outstanding!$b$bLet\'s see if this does the trick....$b$bStand back, $n!',0),
(25604,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Not another one! $n, these devices have been springing up all around Azeroth. We know that they can instigate elemental disturbances in the area, including causing tears in the elemental planes.$B$BThe devices stink of Twilight\'s Hammer. The engravings covering the surface and the captured elemental essence implicate Cho\'gall and his minions are behind this.$B$BIf you find more of these, bring them to me or one of my associates. We need to learn more about what\'s behind this attack.',0),
(25606,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Not another one! $n, these devices have been springing up all around Azeroth. We know that they can instigate elemental disturbances in the area, including causing tears in the elemental planes.$B$BThe devices stink of Twilight\'s Hammer. The engravings covering the surface and the captured elemental essence implicate Cho\'gall and his minions are behind this.$B$BIf you find more of these, please bring them to me or one of my associates. We need to learn more about what\'s behind this attack!',0),
(25607,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, ze junk haz arrived! Zit is ze last piece of ze puzzle! Now to zet it up! Standby, $N!',0),
(25608,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent work, $n.  We might win this one yet.',27326),
(25609,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh yeah! Look at all that booty.$B$BWait a minute... bring it closer!',19116),
(25610,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh yeah! Look at all that booty.$B$BWait a minute... bring it closer!',0),
(25611,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'They\'re moving supplies to Hyjal straight from the elemental planes? That explains so much.$B$BYou\'ve made Goldrinn proud by sealing that flamegate, $N, but there may be more portals to seal. You should check with the other shrines!',0),
(25612,1,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,'They\'re moving supplies to Hyjal straight from the elemental planes? Devious.$B$BYou\'ve made Lo\'Gosh proud by sealing that flamegate, $n, but there may be more portals to seal. You should check with the other shrines!',20253),
(25613,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Kalen sighs.>$B$BWe use guns just fine, friend. CANNONS, on the other hand, I take issue with...',0),
(25614,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent work, $N. The gnome technology, while somewhat obnoxious, is highly effective. We should now have a clear path to Windshear Hold.',0),
(25615,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'With the airways clear our hippogryphs will be able to move into Stonetalon freely. Well done, $N!$B$BNow on to more pressing matters. $B$BWhat you witnessed at Trueshot Point was a small sampling of the decimation left in the wake of Hellscream\'s legacy. As Warchief of the Horde, Hellscream has declared Kalimdor as the Horde\'s sovereign territory. All that would oppose the Horde are destroyed.$B$BWe are Kalimdor\'s last line of defense. Should we fall, Kalimdor will also fall. The Horde must be stopped!',0),
(25616,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'With the Krom\'gar incinerators dealt with, the forest may be allowed to regrow. Only time can heal the wounds left by the Horde.',0),
(25617,2,1,274,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, you are the champion Lo\'Gosh promised! Your eyes don\'t deceive you: you have entered the Firelands, an elemental plane of molten stone and fire. We\'ve got our work cut out for us here.$B$BPut aside your differences with the Alliance, there\'s plenty of danger to go around.$B$BAnd take this: the Fang of Lo\'Gosh will allow you to channel the ancient\'s power here within the Firelands. Use it well!',20253),
(25618,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, you are the champion Goldrinn promised! Your eyes don\'t deceive you: you have entered the Firelands, an elemental plane of molten stone and fire. We\'ve got our work cut out for us here.$B$BPut aside your differences with the Horde, there\'s plenty of danger to go around.$B$BAnd take this: the Fang of Goldrinn will allow you to channel the ancient\'s power here within the Firelands. Use it well!',0),
(25619,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hah! It seems you were right. That broken trident is serving you just fine. I suppose I don\'t get to see you claw anything to death today after all.',0),
(25620,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, my battlemaiden, you\'ve come to me. The warrior caste whispers of nothing but your victories on the battlefield, and we\'ve only just begun our assault to take the city.$B$BYou have served me proud thus far. May the Queen favor you that you might continue to do more of the same.',0),
(25621,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<The Gnomecorder crackles and pops with static electricity.>$B$BCome in, $N. Can you hear me? Zis iz Professor Xakxak!$B$B*POP*$B$B*CRACKLE*$B$BPERFECT! Viz ze Gnomecorder I vill be able to direct you about Stonetalon vile staying out of harmz vay!$B$BNow, onto our next order of buziness!',0),
(25622,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<The Gnomecorder buzzes loudly.>$B$BVonderful! As promised, VOILA, your reward!$B$BNow, I have a bit of news that you might find interesting.',0),
(25623,1,5,274,0,0,0,0,0,'Yes, Goldrinn said you would come. Your eyes do not deceive you: you proved: it turned out; in the Firelands, in the elemental chamber of molten stone and fire. Our business here is simply overwhelming. $B$B Forget about disagreements with the Horde, it\'s hot enough here. $B$B And take this: here, in the Firelands, Goldrinn\'s fang will allow you to direct ancient forces.',19342),
(25624,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, you are the champion Lo\'Gosh promised! Your eyes don\'t deceive you: you have entered the Firelands, an elemental plane of molten stone and fire. We\'ve got our work cut out for us here.$B$BPut aside your differences with the Alliance, there\'s plenty of danger to go around.$B$BAnd take this: the Fang of Lo\'Gosh will allow you to channel the ancient\'s power here within the Firelands. Use it well!',0),
(25626,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Minions of the Old God? Two very potent foes have joined forces then. Their hope to defeat the Tidehunter may not be so foolish after all.$B$B$n, we can\'t let that happen. If Azshara defeats the Tidehunter and takes his power for herself, I\'m not sure any number of us could ever hope to oppose her on the seas.$B$BThe first step is clear at least - we need to hunt down the fiend that destroyed our ships. The navy was confident enough to bring in a new fleet, perhaps they have a plan.',0),
(25627,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Yeah, yeah, yeah... I\'m sure that your little adventure into the cave was very interesting.$B$BHow about we talk about it over drinks back on the Speedbarge once you get me out of this cage?',19116),
(25628,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Yeah, yeah, yeah... I\'m sure that your little adventure into the cave was very interesting.$B$BHow about we talk about it over drinks back on the Speedbarge once you get me out of this cage?',0),
(25629,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, Battlemaiden.$B$BI will attend to the eastern bridge. I need you to attend to the temple itself. The ritual must not be interrupted.',0),
(25630,274,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Can this wait, $c? The battle is not going well.$B$BOh, you\'re here to help. I hope you don\'t mind a little heat...',20253),
(25637,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It is good of you to join me, Battlemaiden. The echoes of your combat graced your approach. It was a beautiful sound to behold.',0),
(25638,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'If he still lives, I may be able to locate this poor soul.',0),
(25640,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good to see you again, $N. Thanks for the rescue in Ashenvale. Damn shame about all the gnomes we lost.$B$BYou ready to get down to business?$B$B<Boog points to \"The Bomb.\">',0),
(25641,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done indeed... I\'d expect nothing less from my own daughter. She\'ll make a fine witch doctor someday.',0),
(25642,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Not too much trouble, I hope. With these samples we should be able to figure out what they plan to do with the ore and the big bomb.',0),
(25643,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<As you reach towards the pedestal, you find it empty. A chill fills the room, and you hear a faint voice...>',0),
(25644,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You were right to come to me with this, $n.  This represents a great threat to us if we do not act swiftly and boldly.',27326),
(25645,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I am a fool...I was misled. This is nothing more than a rusted trinket, and my visions have no doubt been fulfilled.$B$BForgive me, $n. But should you meet this demoness again, I pray you will triumph over her as you did Verinias.',0),
(25646,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Nice job, I could hear their shrill screams from out here. You\'ve turned the whole place on its head!$B$BDid you happen to find any other information about the mining operation?',0),
(25647,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Boog takes the letter from you and begins to examine it.>$B$BInteresting.$B$B<Boog smells the parchment.>$B$BHrm... Troubling...$B$B<Boog folds the paper in half and looks at you.>$B$BCan\'t understand a damn thing written here - if that is writing. Could just be toilet paper. Sure smells like it.',0),
(25648,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good, you\'re here.  Welcome to Azshara, the stage for the next act of the Horde\'s glorious future.  Now get to work. ',0),
(25649,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Minx takes the letter from you and begins to read it.>$B$BUh oh...$B$B<Minx smells the parchment.>$B$BDisgusting!$B$B<Minx folds the paper in half and looks at you.>$B$BThe good news is that this isn\'t toilet paper. The bad news is that the ink on this paper is a mixture of kodo poop and blood. That\'s not the worst of it, though...',0),
(25650,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Beads of sweat roll down Boog\'s overly large forehead as he reads the translated letter.>$B$BThis is bad. Really, really bad. You have to warn Lord Fallowmere at Windshear Hold.$B$BWhat in the... It\'s MOVING! The goblin balloon is taking off! We\'re too late!',0),
(25651,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'My gunpowder!$b$bYou found it! I\'m not crazy after all!',0),
(25652,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Amazing story, $g lad:lass;. I\'d have never believed you had I not seen it with my own eyes. You did enough damage to that balloon to make those fiends pull back! Alas, the threat is far from over. We have only delayed the attack. There is much work to do if we are to stop the Horde from destroying Stonetalon!',0),
(25653,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'By relieving Tortolla of his final burdens you have acquired for us a formidable ally... and the final piece of the puzzle.$B$BSteel yourself, $n. The most difficult part of our journey is to begin.$B$BWe will bring the fight to their stronghold.',27326),
(25654,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'These lands will finally be free of the foulness of the harpies. I cannot thank you enough.',0),
(25655,273,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Thisalee nods, contentedly, her eyes sparkling.>$B$BFeels great to be off the leash, doesn\'t it?',20253),
(25656,1,274,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good, that\'s a start.$B$BThe birds who laid these eggs will never accept them again, so we\'ll have to raise these birds as orphans in the shrine here. Were Aviana here, she never would\'ve let this travesty happen.$B$BBut, on to business...',20253),
(25657,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Amazing!$b$bYou watch the great white beast swim off into the depths and wonder to yourself if anything could ever take him down...',0),
(25658,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The Nar\'shola Wards are performing perfectly. I will inform the Mistress of the Tides of your aid immediately.$B$BThank you for your assistance, my lady. ',0),
(25659,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<The Kvaldir General crumples to the ground, defeated.>$B$B<With this, the ruins of Vashj\'ir have been claimed for Lady Naz\'jar. Her ultimate goals remain uncertain, but it is clear that the naga came here with purpose.>$B$B<If only you could continue, you are sure that the answers to defeating the naga lie within this vision, but the Wavespeaker\'s magics are waning, and you are losing your connection with the Battlemaiden.>',0),
(25660,6,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What ya be wantin\'? Oh no you don\'t. I can see ya got Tony\'s spirit with ya, and I want nothin\' to do with it!',19116),
(25661,11,0,0,0,1000,0,0,0,'<Ajamon makes a face at the state of the organs.>$B$BThey\'s gonna have ta do. It not be like he had many friends. Ain\'t that right, Two-Tusk?',19116),
(25662,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'We don\'t have much time. To get me out of here you are going to have to take out Warlord Roktrog. He holds the key to this prison.',0),
(25663,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<A whispered plea rings within your head.>$B$BTo be born again, but in darkness...$B$BI have been stolen away.$B$B<The spirit appears frantic, but falls silent as her image fades.>',20253),
(25664,273,2,1,0,0,0,0,0,'That was nasty work, $n, but it had to be done.$B$BAnd if Aviana is truly to be resurrected, then perhaps your actions have enabled Blaithe to someday come back as well?$B$BNow let\'s see if we can contact our long lost guardian...',20253),
(25665,1,274,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Slow down, $c! You look as though you\'ve seen a ghost...',20253),
(25667,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Now that you\'ve dealt with the wendigos, we should be able to focus our efforts on the Frostmane trolls to the east.',0),
(25668,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $N. The mountaineers will be glad to hear that half-rations are at an end. They\'ll need all their strength to continue fighting the Frostmanes.',0),
(25669,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'A hero thwarted their plans to destroy Windshear Hold, eh? That hero was you, $N. You are the pride of the Alliance!$B$BIt seems that you have bought us a little bit of time. I must plan for the battle that lies ahead of us. Seek out the other inhabitants of Windshear Hold and lend them your assistance. I will call for you when I am ready to initiate our defensive strategy.',0),
(25670,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This really ain\'t as bad as it looks...',0),
(25671,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good. Their blood is on Hellscream\'s hands. Send enough of them back to Orgrimmar in a body bag and the populace of the Horde might react.$B$B<Lord Fallowmere laughs.>$B$BWho am I kidding? They\'re monsters!',0),
(25672,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh, that\'s disgustin\'!$B$BWe almost there, mon. Just need ta do one more ting!',19116),
(25673,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Alice claps excitedly.>$B$BMr. P you\'re gonna be ok! Hooray!$B$B<Alice expertly places all of the parts you collected into Big Papa.>$B$BOh, Mr. P! I knew it!',0),
(25674,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $R. You\'ve proven that you can take down an ogre... no small feat. Now let\'s see if you can take down an Alliance iron mine...',0),
(25675,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'ve done well today, $n. Not only have you purchased more time before the next ogre attack, but I think you scared some of the captives into working harder.',0),
(25676,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Finally... another operative shows up. I hope you\'re loosened up... it\'s time to tango, partner.',0),
(25677,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'There\'s nothing quite like a big fat kick in the wallet, is there, you Alliance lunkheads?!',0),
(25678,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent work, friend. I like the way you do business.',0),
(25679,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good, you here already. Stick around for a bit, little $R. We gonna mess with the Alliance.$B$BI love my job, mon.',0),
(25680,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'So it was a demon? Those miners never seen a demon before? We\'re in the Blasted Lands, mon! Demons are everywhere!$B$B<Tak\'arili sighs.>$B$BAh well... let\'s get on to da good stuff, shall we?',0),
(25681,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Nice work, mon! Without Hondo, these guys are helpless. Dis mine\'ll be ours soon enough!',0),
(25682,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Okrilla glances over the report.>$B$BImpressive, $n. I wouldn\'t have hidden in that box, but otherwise, you have performed bravely and admirably. The battle we won today may not win us any immediate spoils, but the damage you\'ve done to the Alliance will last for a long time.',0),
(25683,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Okrilla sent you? Okrilla the killa\'?$B$B<Lynnore listens to your tale.>$B$BLoramus was his name? I\'m sorry to say that we have not seen your demon hunter... but we have ways of finding him.',0),
(25684,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent. Now that that\'s out of the way...',0),
(25685,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Lynnore eyes the blood hungrily.>$B$BMore than enough, and still warm! Now, let\'s get this ritual started, shall we?',0),
(25686,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The blood ritual was a success; I can clearly see where Loramus is right now. That is, I can see where the pieces of his body lie...',0),
(25687,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I see... yes, we can work with this.$B$B<Lynnore looks at the night elf\'s head.>$B$BLoramus Thalipedes, demon hunter. I look forward to meeting you.',0),
(25688,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You... you fool! What have you done?',0),
(25689,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What? LORAMUS?!$B$BOh blast, keep it down, would ya? If my boss gets word that I worked for Loramus, do you know how quickly I\'d be on my rear end?!$B$B<Wazzik takes the rune from you, presses it to his chest, closes his eyes, and nods.>$B$BWell, you weren\'t lying. Let\'s get to work.',0),
(25690,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'These are perfect, $n. Lynnore and I will eat well for the next several days.',0),
(25691,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I hope this is what he needs. We probably don\'t have time for you to return and mine any more.',0),
(25692,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'There\'s no doubt about it, you found demon blood.$B$BLoramus\' requests aside, I\'m sure Dar\'toon is thankful for your efforts. They\'ve been struggling to deal with these demon distractions for some time now.',0),
(25693,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is sufficient. If you see Wazzik again, you may tell him that he performed satisfactorily. I will get the bloodmages to work on fashioning the stone knife of sealing. There is no need for questions now. All will be revealed in time.$B$BWhile they work, I have another task for you to complete. Actually, make that three tasks.',0),
(25694,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Your work is appreciated, soldier.$B$B<The warlord leans in close, and whispers:>$B$B$R... if you\'re still interested, I have one more small task for you...',0),
(25695,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'re certain nobody saw you? Good.$B$B<Dar\'toon listens to your recount of the information you saw.>$B$BHmph... fairly harmless stuff. Either the Alliance are foolish enough to NOT be planning something against us... or they\'re hiding their information better than I expected. Either way, well done, soldier.',0),
(25696,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Welcome, traveler. Thank you for responding to my summons.',0),
(25697,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Lynnore examines the amulet.>$B$BHe was an archmage, I can feel it. I will hold the amulet for you while you collect the rest.',0),
(25698,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Lynnore hefts the amulet.>$B$BA warlock... and a powerful one at that. I will hold onto this until the time is right.',0),
(25699,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Lynnore clutches the third amulet.>$B$BHe was a powerful warrior, this one. I will keep the amulet until Loramus is ready to proceed.',0),
(25700,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It would seem that we are prepared to face our demon, $n. We have the amulet\'s blessing, we have the stone knife, and I alone know the demon\'s true name: Rakh\'likh. Together, this may be enough to defeat the Defiler.',0),
(25701,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I see. So this was Loramus\' plan all along.$B$BI suspected correctly, but I suppose I refused to believe it. And now, his final instruction for me makes much more sense:$B$BHe asked me to let you choose from one of these.',0),
(25702,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<The murloc spirit looks upon you sadly.>$B$BSalt-Flop did not shame himself by running away. Look behind me, and see for yourself.$B$BThe Rockpool had no hope against the naga\'s attack.',0),
(25703,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You have done well, brave $C. I am pleased... but I am not yet satisfied.',0),
(25704,6,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Now we gonna bring Tony Two-Tusk back ta life. You both ready, mon?',19116),
(25705,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You make an old murloc proud, $R.$B$BThank you, and may the waves ever lap at your feet.',0),
(25706,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The last Rockpool may be taken hostage today and killed tomorrow, landwalker... but they will pass into the underworld knowing that a brave $R avenged their death. Thank you.',0),
(25708,92,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Enohar takes a sip off of a freshly-refilled mug.>$b$bAye, you\'ve done well, $g lad: lassie;.  You do the Alliance proud.',19116),
(25709,1,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It\'s a tragedy, what happened on the Shattershore.  They weren\'t even soldiers... just people looking for a new home.$b$bI think we\'ve done all we can, $n.',19116),
(25710,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hmm... not bad.  You\'re quicker than many of my men.  Stick around, $n... I may have use of you yet.',19116),
(25711,1,14,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'re an excellent asset to the Alliance and the Kirin Tor, $n.  Well done.$b$bWith time, our forces will retake the mine and press these Horde dogs out of the Blasted Lands.',19116),
(25712,396,396,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you, $n.  Thanks to your efforts, I am confident that with time, we will take back the Nethergarde Mine.',19116),
(25713,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ahh, the sound of things going boom makes my heart pitter-pat.  You\'ve made this gnome\'s day, $n.',19116),
(25714,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'My associates were correct to send you to me.  I have a problem which may threaten the sanctity of Nethergarde, and I need someone more capable than most.',19116),
(25715,274,274,1,0,0,777,777,0,'You saw worgen?  That\'s bad.$b$bWorgen ghosts?  That\'s even worse.$b$bThose weren\'t Horde ships... they were Gilnean.  And they must have been headed down to Surwich, at the bottom of the Tainted Forest.  That makes a lot more sense.$b$bWe\'ve got to try to help them, $n!  The worgen are our allies!',19116),
(25716,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ably done, $n.  Now we see if my suspicions are correct.$b$b<The watcher selects a spell focus and focuses intently on its shadows.  After a moment, he turns back to you with a look of horror on his face.>',19116),
(25717,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you, $n.$B$BI should be a bit more up-front with you. The demons were a nuisance, but they are not the real problem. That worgen druid is our problem.',0),
(25718,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Rohan\'s sending YOU to slay his druid? Very well.$B$BYou should know: Marl Wormthorn is as much demon as he is druid. Even a druid of his power doesn\'t have a chance against the demonic energies that run so deeply through this land. That does not, however, make him any less of an obstacle.',0),
(25719,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Brilliantly done, $n. We have what we need to break the worgen\'s trance.',0),
(25720,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hopefully, with this druid out of the picture, we can get back to our digging. The world is full of powerful artifacts, $n. You just need to be willing to do what it takes to get to them.$B$BFeel free to take one of these. The Reliquary is always happy to share some of its trove with fellow members of the Horde.',0),
(25721,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well I\'ll be. There\'s someone around here that isn\'t a disgrace to Magni, bless his poor gravelly heart.$B$BJust for that, you get first crack at the ale, $glad:lass;. But don\'t let it get to your bloody head! We\'ve got more gorram work to do, and I won\'t tolerate you lettin\' up early!',0),
(25722,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, well. The good news is, these will do perfectly. The bad news is I can tell they\'re the wrong color for topsoil here, even drunk as I am.$B$BThat means things aren\'t looking good for the area, $n. But we\'ve got more tests to run before we hang up the towel.',0),
(25723,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Lovely. These\'ll fry up nice, and the camp\'ll be spared a week of mushroom biscuits.',0),
(25724,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'We should be able to focus our efforts on the rest of the trolls to the east, but there\'s still the matter of the wendigos in the Grizzled Den.',0),
(25725,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'These\'ll do nicely. I\'ll have the lads back on their feet as soon as I make these somewhat edible.',0),
(25726,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh good, it\'s undamaged! Thanks a lot.$B$BYou ah, you might want to wipe yourself off a bit there.',0),
(25727,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good riddance to bad rubbish! I\'ll burn the foul thing later so it doesn\'t stink up the camp.',0),
(25728,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Lord Fallowmere coughs.>$B$BThis is awkward...$B$BGood job out there with the robot. You caught me a little off guard. I didn\'t realize the little girl was so...$B$B<Lord Fallowmere points to his temple and twirls his finger around.>$B$BSpecial...$B$BWell, whatever gets the job done, right? Am I right?$B$BProbably.$B$BHave some ice cream.',0),
(25729,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<The Gnomecorder buzzes loudly.>$B$BVonderful! That\'s von more name I can scratch off of my list!$B$BI vill be in touch.$B$BXakxak, out!',0),
(25730,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well I\'ll be a monkey\'s uncle. You actually got the beast, eh? Well, a deal\'s a deal! Here\'s your reward!',0),
(25731,1,6,0,0,0,0,0,0,'So the harpies are tools of some sort of dragon - \"Sethria.\"$B$BBut what are the dragons doing to those eggs? And what\'s this \'special\' egg that Sethria wanted so badly?$B$BThis is beyond me, $n. I\'ve given a report to Skylord Omnuron - he\'ll know what to do next.',20253),
(25732,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is it?$b$bHow is this gunna remove - wait a minute...',0),
(25733,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good job. I wouldn\'t be surprised if the horrid things had eggs in there somewhere, but it\'ll do for now.',0),
(25734,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Wonderful, $glad:lass;. This should be all we need. Let\'s have a look.',0),
(25735,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Glorious! Beautiful stuff, this ore.$B$BGood on you for not droppin\' your pick. Last person I sent out let the butt end hit the floor, and that part\'s not sparkproof.',0),
(25736,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The thing\'s still got some fight in it! Amazing!$B$BYou\'re a tough one, $n. It\'s much appreciated. I\'d say a reward is in order before you head out.$B$BKeep doin\' your best for Ironforge, you hear? And if you ever see my sister, say hello for me.',0),
(25739,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Captain Kosak forces a smile at you.>$B$BDon\'t worry about me. Should be ok now that big hero killed the spider queen.$B$BCan get reinforcements through safely now.',0),
(25740,6,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, $n! I was hoping to see you out here.$B$BWhat, Omnuron calls this a \'fact-finding mission?\' Bah! Facts are best found on corpses.$B$BLet\'s do some damage.',27326),
(25741,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This will keep us stocked on anti-venom for the foreseeable future. Thank you, $N!',0),
(25743,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh, what might have been...',0),
(25744,1,0,0,0,1000,0,0,0,'<Crazzle gets a gleam in his eye.>$B$BI\'ve got Kravel Koalbeard up there talking to one of their chiefs, but now that you\'re here, we\'ll have the rights to pump up their oil in no time!',19116),
(25745,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Riznek gets a gleam in his eye.>$B$BI\'ve got Trackmaster Zherin up there talking to one of their chiefs, but now that you\'re here, we\'ll have the rights to pump up their oil in no time!',0),
(25746,1,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'re good at this.$B$BI like you.',27326),
(25747,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good to see you again, $C. I almost thought we\'d lost you to the Wavespeaker\'s fool errand.$B$BDid anything come of it?',0),
(25748,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'More naga are amassing to the south than reported too it seems. We shall have to move quickly then.',0),
(25749,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You are perhaps the most dependable person I\'ve ever met. I wish I could have more men half as thorough as you.',0),
(25751,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You are brave indeed! I\'ve seen you battling all manner of murloc, naga, and pointy-toothed fish, but that was nothing! The way you just sling those kelp bulbs under your arm like that is a whole new kind of fearless. BOOM! You could blow up at any second.$B$BYou\'re my kind of $R.',0),
(25752,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You did great up there! You devastated their ranks, but there were far more than we accounted for, and most of our men went down out there in the masses of naga.$B$BWe\'ll need to hold this position as long as possible to buy them time. Hopefully some of them will still make it to the rendezvous.',0),
(25753,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you. Truly.$B$BWe need to get these men moving as soon as possible. I\'ll meet you back at the forward post soon, I\'m sure.',0),
(25754,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Still so many? They must want something very important here to come in such numbers.$B$BI will be honest with you, $n, because you deserve at least that: I don\'t know how much hope there is. We will retreat shortly, but we won\'t be able to defend ourselves when they strike back. We don\'t have anywhere to run... we\'re running out of options.$B$BI\'m sorry, I should keep such thoughts to myself. Do me a favor and don\'t mention any of that to the men. I\'ll figure something out.',0),
(25755,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'re finished! Just in time. I don\'t think we could have held them much longer.$B$BAn artifact? Could this be something we can use against the naga? I suppose that would require finding it.$B$BWe may have to attend to more pressing matters first, until an opportunity to pursue this further presents itself.',0),
(25756,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What?! How\'d they get that much gold to offer?$B$BWe don\'t have that kind of money!',19116),
(25757,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What?! How\'d they get that much gold to offer?$B$BWe don\'t have that kind of money!',0),
(25758,1,5,274,0,0,0,0,0,'Look at these things. Ugh, the runes make my eyes hurt. This one here is meant to sear flesh? Seriously? Ouch! Wait a minute...$B$BThese plates are designed to be riveted directly into flesh. The pain must be unbearable!',27326),
(25759,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Not another one! $n, these devices have been springing up all around Azeroth. We know that they can instigate elemental disturbances in the area, including causing tears in the elemental planes.$B$BThe devices stink of Twilight\'s Hammer. The engravings covering the surface and the captured elemental essence implicate Cho\'gall and his minions are behind this.$B$BIf you find more of these, please bring them to me or one of my associates. We need to learn more about what\'s behind this attack.',0),
(25760,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'A Battlemaiden? I never heard of such a thing.$B$BThe way you explain it, it sounds like the naga forces are far greater in scope than the Admiral could possibly have realized. We might be able to learn more through the blade if we can find other locations where this Battlemaiden was present, but the information you gave me makes me fear for the admiral and his soldiers. We must warn them.',0),
(25761,6,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'That was some fancy bladework, $n!$B$BThere\'s one less threat for us to worry about in Hyjal.',27326),
(25762,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You did this favor to ingratiate yourself with me, but I will not sing your praises.$B$BI know what is to come. Where the sea failed, the great air spirit will strike you and your people down for your many transgressions against the elements.$B$BBegone from my sight!',19116),
(25763,6,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,'They\'re doing what?$B$BThey\'re cloaking something? Of course - so our aerial scouts can\'t see anything with our eagle-eyes!',27326),
(25764,4,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'We did it, $n! Aviana\'s Egg should soon be tucked safely in the boughs of her shrine.$B$BDo you think this means she\'ll really return to us?',27326),
(25765,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Kosak sent you, eh? Surprising. I thought for sure that he\'d be dead by now.$B$BWell if you made it past the blockade then you definitely have something that we can use.$B$BNow, do you have any news of the Horde? What are they doing? Where are they going? Tell me everything.',0),
(25766,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I assure you, simpleton, the spirits you captured are at rest. Do not let their protests move you.',0),
(25767,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Wonderful! Arcanist Valdurian will be most pleased.',0),
(25768,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I\'m assuming you saw the Krom\'gar hot air balloon on your way here. If not, get your eyes checked. It\'s hovering directly over the oil platform.',0),
(25769,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good to see you again, $N. I have some news from Mirkfallon Lake.',0),
(25770,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hah! Nice to see those addlebrained mountaineers knew to hand the ale off to a real man to get the job done.$B$BWelcome to my survey. If you\'re of the mind to help Ironforge by takin\' over the intended jobs of some useless, lazy sods that call themselves dwarves, you\'re in the right place!',0),
(25771,1,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Just a shard?  Pfuh!  This gets me nothing!  Take your reward and get out of my sight.$B$BSounds familiar?  It should, because I say it a thousand times per day.$B$BOh how I loathe this world.\n',19116),
(25772,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Simply amazing.  I had doubted that anyone could find another sphere, yet here it is, pulsating in my hands.$B$BWell done, $n!$B$BShould you find anymore--and I believe this to be an impossibility--return them to me and I shall reward you again.',19116),
(25773,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Yes, $n, this shard does explain the occurrence of the rift. The elemental planes have been in chaos in Outland ever since Draenor was destroyed. These shards cause a weakness in the already damaged elemental planes and allow the elementals to cross into our world$B$BWe\'re still looking into how these rifts are appearing in Azeroth. Keep bringing us the shards. Every shard we get brings us closer to understanding how these rifts are appearing.',0),
(25774,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Genius! Now, where\'s that gold paint? I know it\'s around here somewhere.',19116),
(25775,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Genius! Now, where\'s that gold paint? I know it\'s around here somewhere.',0),
(25776,4,5,1,0,0,0,0,0,'Sethria is slain! I knew it was worth the risk.$B$BI\'ll stay here to look for survivors, but I imagine they\'ll want to see you back at the shrine.',27326),
(25777,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Let\'s take a look here.$B$BOh, this is just lovely. \"Significant geological instabilities\"? \"Threat of sudden, massive topological destabilization\"?$B$BNice to hear that somethin\' bad might happen around here. I guess we\'ll just pick up our flooded town and fly it off somewhere safe!$B$BBah!',0),
(25778,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Just put it down on the ground, $r.',19116),
(25779,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Just put it down on the ground, $R.',0),
(25780,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'He\'s dead! Thank the Makers...$B$BI don\'t like the looks of them, lad. The Dark Iron I\'ve tussled with were never this crazy. Something\'s getting to these sods...',0),
(25781,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Not another one! $n, these devices have been springing up all around Azeroth. We know that they can instigate elemental disturbances in the area, including causing tears in the elemental planes.$B$BThe devices stink of Twilight\'s Hammer. The engravings covering the surface and the captured elemental essence implicate Cho\'gall and his minions are behind this.$B$BIf you find more of these, please bring them to me or one of my associates. We need to learn more about what\'s behind this attack.',0),
(25782,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Not another one! $n, these devices have been springing up all around Azeroth. We know that they can instigate elemental disturbances in the area, including causing tears in the elemental planes.$B$BThe devices stink of Twilight\'s Hammer. The engravings covering the surface and the captured elemental essence implicate Cho\'gall and his minions are behind this.$B$BIf you find more of these, please bring them to me or one of my associates. We need to learn more about what\'s behind this attack.',0),
(25783,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Not another one! $n, these devices have been springing up all around Azeroth. We know that they can instigate elemental disturbances in the area, including causing tears in the elemental planes.$B$BThe devices stink of Twilight\'s Hammer. The engravings covering the surface and the captured elemental essence implicate Cho\'gall and his minions are behind this.$B$BIf you find more of these, please bring them to me or one of my associates. We need to learn more about what\'s behind this attack.',0),
(25784,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Not another one! $n, these devices have been springing up all around Azeroth. We know that they can instigate elemental disturbances in the area, including causing tears in the elemental planes.$B$BThe devices stink of Twilight\'s Hammer. The engravings covering the surface and the captured elemental essence implicate Cho\'gall and his minions are behind this.$B$BIf you find more of these, please bring them to me or one of my associates. We need to learn more about what\'s behind this attack.',0),
