(28824,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Therazane\'s eyes appear slightly more crystalline than you recall.>$B$BOzruk has been reclaimed by the earth.$B$BTake your reward and leave me be, $n. I wish to be left alone.',0),
(28825,396,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'May your sense of honor and duty serve Azeroth well, $c.',19342),
(28826,6,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Now that your eyes have seen the truth, where will you choose to serve?',19342),
(28827,1,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,'All of our war ships are off fighting the Horde. You\'ll have to take the mercenary ship.',15595),
(28828,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Nice. Eggs.$b$bThese will go great with a little bear bacon.  Hey Francis, got any bear meat left over?',0),
(28829,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'My honor is restored.$b$bPartially.$b$bMy tale continues, $c, for I have left portions of my honor elsewhere in this forest.$b$bIt has not been a very easy journey for me.',0),
(28830,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Be glad that the adult giants are trapped on the other side of that gorge. They are far hardier than these tumblers you fight.$b$bI feel rejuvenated by your courage, $c. Perhaps all hope is not lost after all...',0),
(28831,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'If I survive my wounds, I will always remember your name, $c.$b$bWhenever the wind whistles through the trees, I will always hear your name.$b$bThank you.',0),
(28832,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You two are the last thing I expected to see fall from the sky. Highbank is under attack!',0),
(28833,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What is this? You... rescuing me?$b$b<Erunak smiles at you.>$b$bThis will take some getting used to.',15595),
(28834,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What is this? You... rescuing me?$B$B<Erunak smiles at you.>$B$BThis will take some getting used to.',0),
(28836,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $n!$B$BKnow that without your aid, things would be far different here.$B$BNot only would I be long dead, but the naga and their allies would have free reign over the sea.$B$BThe king himself shall hear of your heroism in this realm.',0),
(28837,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Let\'s see what I can do with these...',0),
(28838,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good. It is just as Jaron described it.',0),
(28839,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The dreamcatcher is charged.  We are nearly ready to retake Mazthoril.',0),
(28840,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Haleh applies the water to your dreamcatcher.>$b$bYou\'ve done well, $N.',0),
(28841,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It will take some time for Mazthoril to recover... but she will.$b$bThe blue dragonflight is far from dead.',0),
(28842,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You have our thanks, $N.',0),
(28843,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hellscream shall know of your deeds here, $n.$b$bWithout you, things here would be far worse.$b$bLok\'tar ogar, my friend!',15595),
(28845,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You actually came here looking for me?',0),
(28847,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You are $N, yes?$b$bGood, you will serve well. I require the aid of a $c such as yourself.',0),
(28848,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Umbranse... I see. I will carry this information onto my people.$b$bYou will be contacted if you are needed again.',0),
(28849,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Another $c for the Highlands? Here, sign this indemnification waiver...',15595),
(28850,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Greymane\'s right.  These beasts do not give a damn about our politics.$B$BGilneas needs to stand together.',25549),
(28852,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'This is great news, $n! I\'m glad our drakes were able to assist you. Thank you for rescuing them from the clutches of Twilight\'s Hammer.',0),
(28853,1,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Tooranu looks over the documents you discovered.>$B$BIt\'s all here, $N. Details of how the cult is tearing up the Highlands, who they\'ve sent, where they are, and what they plan to do. Invaluable.$B$BI shall distribute this knowledge to the rest of the Earthen Ring at once. Thank you, friend.',15595),
(28854,1,274,0,0,0,0,0,0,'So it is done.$B$BWould that I could bring this entire mountain down upon itself, I would.',15595),
(28856,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Welcome to Cenarion Hold.$b$b<Windcaller Proudhorn brushes some snow off of your shoulder.>$b$bYou\'ve certainly come from far off.',0),
(28857,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'For decades has the garrison at Nethergarde held firm against the threat of the Horde and we do not intend to surrender now.',0),
(28858,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Our enemies are numerous, $C. It will take skill and bravery to overcome them all.',0),
(28859,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Welcome to Cenarion Hold, traveler.',0),
(28860,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Aye, that\'s how it\'s done! With heroes like you taking care of business, I\'m proud to be a part of the Alliance.',0),
(28861,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh aye, quite a haul!$B$BThis\'ll last me until... oh say probably tomorrow.',0),
(28862,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh hey, yer just in time! I was working up a huge appetite, workin\' so hard to feed these hungry refugees. Yessir.',0),
(28863,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Grim business, but well done all the same. Thank you, $n.',0),
(28864,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Go figure. Never thought I\'d develop a taste for imported draft. Thanks, $n!',0),
(28865,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Silithus, such a worthless piece of land. It is a wonder that the great cataclysm did not sunder it fully!',0),
(28866,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It\'s about time they sent someone to help.$B$BMillhouse Manastorm?  It sounds like we\'re both after the same person.',19342),
(28867,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Silithus, not such a great place, eh? We get a lot of you from there...',0),
(28868,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $N. That\'ll teach them not to mess with us in our home!',0),
(28869,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Pebble seems quite happy to meet you.>',0),
(28870,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Hail, $n. Nadun spoke highly of you.$B$BAre you here to aid us?',0),
(28871,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Look what we have here! A single Horde $C can demolish the Wildhammer by the dozen. What hope do they have now?',0),
(28872,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Yes, yes. Burn them out, as you would flush groundhogs from their holes...$B$BWell done, $n.',0),
(28873,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Griff greedily snatches the heap of food, enough to feed dozens of men.>$B$BGreat! This\'ll tide me over for ... hours!',0),
(28874,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You made that look easy, $n.$B$BGet the Wildhammer off of their mounts and they\'re nothing!',0),
(28875,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'The High Shaman has been brought down! Thundermar will no doubt try to send others, but on this day, the Dragonmaw are triumphant.',0),
(28876,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You\'re the reinforcements that Thork sent?$B$BYou\'ll do fine as long you can kill night elves. The forest is crawling with them.',0),
(28877,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I suppose my reputation grows. Yes, yes I kill harpies. I don\'t enjoy it. But their raids on our supply caravans must cease, and someone\'s got to organize a resistance.',0),
(28878,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'A small tag on this present reads:$B$BHappy holidays, $n!',0),
(28879,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It sounds like little Roo had a great time this week. I know he was getting awfully lonely in the orphanage and was eager to make some new friends. Thank you so much for agreeing to look after him.',0),
(28880,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you for agreeing to care for Kekek this week. I know he can be a handful, but I think that with more individual attention and a few more friends, he\'ll do a lot better. No doubt he\'s going to be telling stories of his adventures with you for weeks.',0),
(28881,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What, you here to help?',0),
(28882,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'What\'s that smell?  Ah.....Smells like victory.  Your efforts in Tol Barad are a great triumph for the entire Alliance, your contributions will not be forgotten.',15595),
(28884,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You bring word of victory, just as I expected!  Any triumph in Tol Barad is in turn a triumph for the Horde.  Have no doubt, your efforts here will be rewarded.',15595),
(28885,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh no! My weapons and totems!$B$BThey\'re destroyed!!!',0),
(28909,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Sauranok nods toward you.>$B$B$C.',0),
