(32106,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'A small tag on this present reads:$B$BHappy holidays, $n!',0),
(32108,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<This fire will signal the full might of the Horde invasion fleet to land on this beach, beginning Garrosh\'s campaign in Pandaria.>',0),
(32109,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'<Blue sails are barely visible on the horizon - the full might of the Alliance fleet, awaiting one final signal.>',0),
(32115,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ye\' did good work out there. It\'s not right seein\' the dead unable to rest like that.',0),
(32116,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oi! We got a right nasty problem here. Kicked the hornet\'s nest. Except these are mogu ghost hornets with a mean streak a bloody mile wide!',0),
(32118,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah, yes. Good. Help from Belloc. He never does like to get his hands dirty.',0),
(32119,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good work! Now maybe the workers can get through a day without fillin\' their britches!',0),
(32120,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good, good. We\'ll begin our research post-haste.',0),
(32121,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Those things are nasty! Thanks for takin\' care of \'em for us.',0),
(32122,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You did it! Good work! Really saved our bacon!$B$BHere\'s to hoping those things don\'t come back...',0),
(32123,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, $n. I see your time in this land has hardened your resolve and sharpened your skills.',0),
(32126,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Just remember, the weapon of choice is not always the weapon with the longest range or heaviest amount of damage. In the end, the best weapon is the weapon that works every time.',0),
(32127,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It is not enough to rob the Alliance of their leaders. We must warn those who would aspire to leadership the cost of such ambition.',0),
(32128,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ah! Look at them burn. These new Alliance craft require more to destroy them permanently however. I am sure they will have those fires out in a day or two.',0),
(32130,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good and waxy, just like they asked for. Here\'s your share.',0),
(32131,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Ha! YES! You got me some! I\'m gonna make the best bomb EVER!$B$BMan I love bombs! Love making them, love blowin\' em up...$B$B... and yeah, that IS how I got this eyepatch. What\'s it to ya?',0),
(32132,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good work. That should slow them down by a few days, at least.$B$BYou don\'t win the war by playing the short game, friend. Trust me, this is the right strategy.',0),
(32133,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good work, $n. I\'ve already been getting some useful information that should help make our next offensive even more devastating.',0),
(32134,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh heck yeah! That\'ll show \'em that NOBODY blows stuff up like goblins blow stuff up!$B$BOh, and you did good work too.',0),
(32135,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Cut off the head, and the body will fall.$B$B... Unless you\'re forsaken, I guess. I realize I should probably stop using that saying now that I am.',0),
(32136,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'More fuel huh? Is her \"loveliness\" afraid she might have to do a little more than sit around lookin\' pretty?',0),
(32137,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Oh, yuck! Why are these barrels wet?! Oh nevermind! At least you got here before they made me work. I can\'t think of anything more horrible!',0),
(32138,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good for nothin\' huh?! I\'m busting my rump down here!$B$BMaybe her \"uselessness\" would like to come down here and haul this lumber herself!',0),
(32139,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'It\'s about time you showed up with this lumber order! I was just about to come down there and get it myself.',0),
(32140,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Is she still complaining about diamonds and rubies? We found something better than diamonds down here!$B$BThis ore is special. It has power!',0),
(32141,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Did they manage to find anything useful down there? Maybe an emerald or an opal? Is it too much to ask for a little bit of effort?!$B$BNevermind! I\'ll make sure this shipment gets where it\'s goin\'.',0),
(32142,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Well done, soldier. That should help keep the horde in check.',0),
(32144,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thanks to your actions, the Horde knows it cannot feed its troops.$B$BThe timeframe they can withstand a siege is greatly reduced and their morale is going to start suffering soon.$B$BWe just need to keep applying pressure.',0),
(32145,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Great work! Sorry to put good soldiers in harms way but my Auto-Demolish-o-Tronic Mk 2 isn\'t functional yet.',0),
(32146,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Thank you soldier. That should teach the Horde that it will take more than a couple of mooks to scare us away.',0),
(32148,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good work, soldier. Without those shamans, I don\'t think they\'ll have much luck breaking down our defenses.',0),
(32149,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Good work! With this, we\'ll be able to finish reinforcing the structure of the keep, which will help keep people safe. You\'ve saved lives today!',0),
(32150,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Without those supplies, they won\'t be able to support bringing more warriors in the fight. If they can\'t bring in more warriors, we have a great shot at holding out.$B$BFor today, at least.',0),
(32151,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Alright! We\'ll get that stone mortared into the cracks in our walls faster than a Dwarf downs a pint.',0),
(32152,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You really showed them who owns this beach, $n. Good work!',0),
(32153,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'I know it wasn\'t easy, but you did it. Good work. You\'ve got my respect, soldier.',0),
(32154,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Wish I could\'ve been there to watch their fuel burn! Probably put on quite the show.$B$BYou\'ve done well, $n!',0),
(32156,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You have done these soldiers a great service, $n. The only thing left to do is make sure they did not die in vain.',0),
(32157,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent work, $C! Eventually we will wipe the Horde from this continent.',0),
(32158,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Excellent work, $n! Now the forest can begin its regrowth process. From all death comes new life, and a new opportunity to protect it.',0),
(32161,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You place the feathers in the dirt, then look off in the direction of the temple...',0),
(32162,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'You lay the meat out atop the trap, then turn your eyes toward the jungle...',0),
